var FT={"Aberrant Spawn":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Advantage against Charm and mind reading, Psychic Resistance, and a tentacle Unarmed Strike.","full":"**Aberrant Mind.** You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Charmed condition and against any effect that would read your thoughts.\n**Psychic Resistance.** You have Resistance to Psychic damage.\n**Tentacle.** One of your limbs is a rubbery tentacle you can strike with. You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls with your Unarmed Strike. When you deal damage with it, you can deal Bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier instead of the normal damage.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"res":["Psychic"],"notes":[["Advantage","Saves to avoid or end Charmed, and against effects that read your thoughts (Aberrant Spawn)"],["Note","Aberrant Spawn: tentacle Unarmed Strike uses Dex or Str, 1d6 + mod Bludgeoning"]]}},"Ace Pilot":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Piloting proficiency or Expertise, 1,000 ft move on Evasive Maneuvers, Advantage on ship melee attacks as Pilot.","full":"**Expert Pilot.** You gain proficiency in the Piloting skill. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it.\n**Hard Turn.** When you take the Evasive Maneuvers action, you can move the ship up to 1,000 feet in any direction.\n**Ramming Maneuver.** As the Pilot, you have Advantage on attack rolls with ship Melee weapons.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it.","fx":{"notes":[["Proficiency","Piloting, or Expertise in it if already proficient (Ace Pilot)"],["Advantage","Attack rolls with ship Melee weapons as Pilot (Ace Pilot)"]]}},"Adamantine Clan":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Dwarves. Unarmored AC is 10 + Dex + Con (a Shield is allowed). Critical Hits against you become normal hits.","full":"**Adamantine Skin.** While you wear no armor, your base Armor Class is 10 plus your Dexterity modifier plus your Constitution modifier. You can still use a Shield and keep this benefit.\n**Adamantine Bones.** Any Critical Hit against you becomes a normal hit.","pre":"Dwarf","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Adamantine Clan: with no armor, AC = 10 + Dex + Con (Shield allowed). Critical Hits against you become normal hits"]]}},"Affluent":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Origin feat. An Uncommon magic item from the DM and 100 CR, plus another 100 CR with each new level.","full":"**Heirloom.** You gain an Uncommon magic item chosen by the DM, handed down in your family. A Bag of Holding or Cloak of Protection is a good fit.\n**Stipend.** You gain 100 CR, and another 100 CR each time you gain a character level after that."},"Android":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. No need for food, drink, air or sleep, 4 hour Long Rest, Machine Code language and Technomancy, and a skill.","full":"You are an escaped android, almost a perfect copy of a human with wiring hidden under the skin. You may not even know what you are.\n**Construct Anatomy.** You do not need food, drink or air. You do not need to sleep, and magic cannot put you to sleep. You can finish a Long Rest in 4 hours if you spend them motionless and conscious.\n**Machine Code.** You know Machine Code, the language of machines, and the Technomancy cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it (choose when you take the feat).\n**Technical Expertise.** You gain proficiency in Data, Piloting or Technology, your choice.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"langs":["Machine Code"],"notes":[["Proficiency","One of Data, Piloting or Technology (Android)"],["Note","Android: no need for food, drink, air or sleep. Long Rest in 4 hours while motionless"]]}},"Aquanaut":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Breathe underwater, Swim Speed equal to your Speed, and simple talk with swimming creatures.","full":"**Aquatic.** You can breathe underwater.\n**Finned.** You have a Swim Speed equal to your Speed.\n**Marine Speech.** You can pass simple ideas to any Beast, Elemental or Monstrosity that has a Swim Speed. It understands your words, but you gain no special ability to understand it.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Aquanaut: breathe underwater, Swim Speed equal to your Speed"]]}},"Arcane Cannoneer":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Add Proficiency Bonus to Mega cantrip damage. Once per rest, impose Disadvantage on a save against your Mega spell.","full":"**Mega Cantrip.** When you use the Gunner action to magnify a damaging cantrip to Mega scale, you can add your Proficiency Bonus to its damage roll.\n**Over-Cast.** When you cast a Mega spell that forces a save, you can give one target Disadvantage on the save. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it."},"Astrogations Inc.: Starguide":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Once per Long Rest, flip a d20 to its opposite face. 50 percent off Star Charts from Astrogations Inc.","full":"**Momentary Prescience.** When you roll a d20 for a D20 Test, you can flip the die over and use the number on the bottom. On a balanced d20 the top and bottom add up to 21. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.\n**Navigator's Discount.** You get a 50 percent discount on Star Charts you buy from Astrogations Inc.\n**Faction Feat.** The DM can grant a Faction feat when you join a faction or finish a quest for it. It can also replace the feat from your background."},"Battleframe Dragoon":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Advantage against Mega creatures once per turn, drop to 1 Mega HP and strike back once per rest, and a path to the Oni rank.","full":"**Kaiju Slayer.** Once on each of your turns, you can gain Advantage on an attack roll against a Mega creature.\n**Relentless Retaliation.** When you are the Pilot of a Battleframe that drops to 0 Mega Hit Points, it can stay at 1 Mega Hit Point instead. You can then make one melee attack with a frame weapon as a Reaction. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**One Hundred to Oni.** Keep a count of the enemies you reduce to 0 Hit Points. At 100 you earn the rank of Oni and gain the Faction feat Lakshay: Oni.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it."},"Beastperson":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Advantage on Dex saves while Bloodied and a claw Unarmed Strike dealing Slashing damage.","full":"You may look like any kind of beast, from a cat's ears and tail to something close to a lycanthrope.\n**Animalistic Reflexes.** You have Advantage on Dexterity saving throws while you are Bloodied.\n**Claws.** Your sharp claws are a weapon. You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls with your Unarmed Strike. When you deal damage with it, you can deal Slashing damage equal to 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier instead of the normal damage.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"notes":[["Advantage","Dexterity saves while Bloodied (Beastperson)"],["Note","Beastperson: claw Unarmed Strike uses Dex or Str, 1d6 + mod Slashing"]]}},"Clown":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Performance, a reroll of low d20s, and Vicious Mockery that can knock targets Prone.","full":"You come from Circus Maximus, where clowns are pale humans with red noses and a love of mischief.\n**Natural Entertainer.** You gain proficiency in Performance.\n**Pratfall.** When you roll a 5 or lower on the d20 for a D20 Test, you can reroll it and must use the new roll. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Vicious Shenanigans.** You learn the Vicious Mockery cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it (choose when you take the feat). When a creature fails its save against this spell and rolls a 5 or lower on the d20, it has the Prone condition.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"skills":["Performance"]}},"Blaster Master (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Dex. Bonus damage on matching blaster dice, ignore the DM-C property, and a ranged blaster attack after Dash or Disengage.","full":"Raise Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Blaster Roulette.** If two damage dice you roll for a blaster show the same number, you deal bonus damage equal to that number. You can add this bonus only once per turn.\n**Ignore Cooldown.** You ignore the DM-C property of weapons.\n**Run and Gun.** When you take the Dash or Disengage action, you can make a ranged attack with a blaster as a Bonus Action.","pre":"Level 4+, Dex 13+","asi":["DEX"]},"Brutal Grip":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Str. Wield a Two-Handed melee weapon in one hand, and a Versatile one in one hand counts as Light.","full":"Raise Strength by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Heavy Duelist.** You can wield a Melee weapon that has the Two-Handed property in one hand.\n**Versatile Dual Wielder.** While you wield a Melee weapon that has the Versatile property in one hand, it has the Light property for you.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+","asi":["STR"]},"Chief Engineer":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Technology proficiency or Expertise, stronger Emergency Repairs, and a shield for the Pilot's mental saves.","full":"**Technology Expert.** You gain proficiency in Technology. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it.\n**Advanced Repairs.** When you take the Emergency Repairs action, you can choose a DC 20 check instead of DC 15. On a success the ship regains an extra 10 Mega Hit Points.\n**Ship Firewall.** While you are the Engineer, the Pilot has Advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom and Charisma saves made on the ship's behalf.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it.","fx":{"skills":["Technology"],"notes":[["Proficiency","Expertise in Technology if already proficient (Chief Engineer)"]]}},"Chronomancy Initiate":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Learn Moment to Think, add Chronomancy spells to your list, and keep Proficiency Bonus many of them always prepared.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Cantrip.** You learn the Moment to Think cantrip.\n**Expanded Spell List.** Spells with the Chronomancy tag join your spell list. Haste, Slow and Time Stop have that tag.\n**Prepared Spells.** Choose a number of Chronomancy spells equal to your Proficiency Bonus. They are always prepared for you. When you gain a level, you can swap one of them for a different Chronomancy spell.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Church of the Sun Above: Adherent":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Religion proficiency and an extra 1d8 Radiant damage on a hit, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"**Dogma.** You gain proficiency in Religion.\n**Solar Judgement.** When you damage a creature with a weapon, a spell or an Unarmed Strike, you can deal an extra 1d8 Radiant damage to it. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses when you finish a Long Rest.\n**Faction Feat.** The DM can grant a Faction feat when you join a faction or finish a quest for it. It can also replace the feat from your background.","fx":{"skills":["Religion"]}},"Creative":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Origin feat. Heroic Inspiration from a natural 20 on an ability check, and room for two Heroic Inspirations.","full":"**Innovation.** When you roll a 20 on the d20 for an ability check, you gain Heroic Inspiration. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Double Inspiration.** You can hold two instances of Heroic Inspiration at once. You can spend only one on each roll."},"Cyberfiend":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Tieflings. Metal claws that deal Necrotic damage, and a 15 foot teleport as a Bonus Action.","full":"Your birth was warped by the Foulest Abyss of the mechademons.\n**Cyber Claw.** Retractable metal claws sit in your fingers. You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of Strength for attack and damage rolls with your Unarmed Strike. When you deal damage with it, you can deal Necrotic damage equal to 1d6 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier instead of the normal damage.\n**Translocator.** As a Bonus Action, you can light the circuits under your skin and teleport up to 15 feet to a space you can see. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses when you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest.","pre":"Tiefling"},"DD&D: Artifactor":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Attune to four magic items, and cast Identify free with an appraisal of the item's value.","full":"You work for DD&D as an Artifactor, finding valuable magic items by sharp dealing or bold expeditions.\n**Additional Attunement.** You can attune to up to four magic items instead of three.\n**Eye for Quality.** You can cast Identify without a spell slot or components. When you do, you also learn the item's market value in Credits.\n**Faction Feat.** The DM can grant a Faction feat when you join a faction or finish a quest for it. It can also replace the feat from your background.","fx":{"notes":[["Note","DD&D: Artifactor: attune to up to four magic items"]]}},"Demolitionist":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Str or Dex. Make a free grenade each Long Rest, a better save DC for bombs, and throw a grenade in place of an attack.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Grenade.** When you finish a Long Rest, you can make one Concussion Grenade, Flashbang or Freeze Bomb. It lasts until your next Long Rest, then falls apart harmlessly.\n**Improved Ordinance.** Your Bomb, Bottled Lightning, Concussion Grenade, Flashbang and Freeze Bomb use this save DC if it is higher: 8 plus the modifier of the ability this feat raised plus your Proficiency Bonus.\n**Quick Grenade.** When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with throwing a Concussion Grenade, Flashbang or Freeze Bomb.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+ or Dex 13+","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Dilettante":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Humans and Near-Humans. Each Long Rest, gain a weapon, skill or tool proficiency, or a Cleric, Druid or Wizard cantrip.","full":"When you finish a Long Rest, you gain proficiency in one weapon, skill or tool of your choice, or you temporarily learn one cantrip from the Cleric, Druid or Wizard spell list. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for that cantrip (choose when you take the feat). You keep the proficiency or cantrip until you finish a Long Rest.","pre":"Human or Near-Human"},"Dogfighter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Make an attack miss with a Barrel Roll when your Fighter would drop to 0 Mega HP, and Advantage on Targeted Strike.","full":"**Barrel Roll.** When an attack would reduce your ship to 0 Mega Hit Points while you are the Pilot, you can use your Reaction to perform a Barrel Roll, and the attack misses. You can do this only in a Fighter. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Precision Strike.** You have Advantage on attack rolls when you take the Targeted Strike action.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it."},"Exomorph":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Skathari. +2 AC at full Hit Points, eat almost anything, and shed your shell to end a condition.","full":"**Armored Exoskeleton.** While you have all your Hit Points, you gain a +2 bonus to AC.\n**Eat Anything.** You get nourishment from any organic matter. Inorganic matter gives none, but you can eat anything softer than stone without harm.\n**Molt.** As a Bonus Action, you can shed your exoskeleton to remove one or more of these conditions from yourself: Blinded, Deafened, Grappled, Poisoned, Prone or Restrained. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Skathari","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Exomorph: +2 AC while you have all your Hit Points"]]}},"Field Commander":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Cha. Command an ally within 60 feet to use a Reaction action, and enemies cannot gain Advantage against you next to two allies.","full":"Raise Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Command.** As an action, you can command an ally within 60 feet that can hear you. The ally immediately takes an action as a Reaction. That action can only be Attack (one attack only), Dash, Dodge, Hide, Influence, Search, Study or Utilize. If the ally takes Dash this way, its benefits last until the end of the ally's next turn.\n**Tight Formation.** While you are within 5 feet of two or more allies who do not have the Incapacitated condition, enemies cannot have Advantage on attack rolls against you.","pre":"Level 4+, Cha 13+","asi":["CHA"]},"Flex Caster (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Spend an extra slot to raise a spell's level by 1, or cast at base level from a higher slot and regain a level 1 slot.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Upcast.** When you cast a spell that can use a higher-level slot, such as Magic Missile, you can spend one additional spell slot to raise its effective level by 1.\n**Downcast.** When you cast a spell with a higher-level slot, you can recycle the extra energy instead of boosting the spell. The spell is cast at its base level and you regain one expended level 1 spell slot.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Focused Critical":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes score a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Improved Critical.** Your attack rolls with weapons and Unarmed Strikes score a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20 on the d20.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["STR","DEX"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Focused Critical: weapon and Unarmed Strike attacks crit on 19-20"]]}},"Galactic Bank: Trustee":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. A line of credit that grows with level and 20 percent off items worth 100 CR or less.","full":"You hold the title of Trustee and a Platinum Member account at the Galactic Bank.\n**Line of Credit.** You can spend Credits you lack through a line of credit. It starts at 1,000 CR and rises at character level 5 (10,000 CR), 11 (50,000 CR) and 17 (100,000 CR). Every ten days you go without paying back what you owe, the debt grows by 100 CR.\n**Platinum Member Discounts.** When you buy an item worth 100 CR or less, you get a 20 percent discount.\n**Faction Feat.** The DM can grant a Faction feat when you join a faction or finish a quest for it. It can also replace the feat from your background."},"Gambler (Dark Matter)":{"tools":"Dice Set, Dragonchess Set, Playing Card Set, Three-Dragon Ante Set","cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Origin feat. Gaming Set proficiency, Advantage on games of chance, and turn a roll into a 20 after three low rolls in a row.","full":"**Gaming Sets.** You gain proficiency with all Gaming Sets and have Advantage on ability checks for games of chance.\n**Losing Streak.** Record each time you roll a 9 or lower on the d20 for a D20 Test. Roll and record the d20s for Advantage and Disadvantage one after another. After three or more such rolls in a row, you can change a d20 roll to a 20. An attack roll changed this way is not a Critical Hit. Once you use this, discard your recorded rolls.","fx":{"notes":[["Proficiency","All Gaming Sets (Gambler)"]]}},"Grafter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Extra Arm and Internal graft slots, a d4 to missed graft weapon attacks, free first installs, and faster Construct graft installs.","full":"Raise Strength, Dexterity or Constitution by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Extra Slots.** You have two Arm graft slots and two Internal graft slots, and can install a graft in each.\n**Machine Precision.** When you miss with a weapon installed as a graft, such as an Arm Cannon or Embedded Weapon, you can roll 1d4 and add it to the attack roll, which may turn the miss into a hit. You can use this once per turn, a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and regain all uses when you finish a Long Rest.\n**Painless Attachment.** You lose no Hit Points or Hit Point Dice the first time you install a graft in a given body slot.\n**Quick Installation.** You can install a Construct graft on your body with the Utilize action.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["STR","DEX","CON"]},"Grax's Guys for Cheap: Grax's Guy":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Heroic Inspiration on a natural 1 on a save, plus one skill, one tool and one language.","full":"Grax's Guys are known for being tough and dependable.\n**Plucky.** When you roll a 1 on the d20 for a saving throw, you gain Heroic Inspiration. You cannot use it to reroll that same save.\n**Work Experience.** You gain proficiency in one skill and one tool of your choice, and you learn one language of your choice.\n**Faction Feat.** The DM can grant a Faction feat when you join a faction or finish a quest for it. It can also replace the feat from your background.","pick":[{"k":"sk","t":"skills","n":1,"from":["Acrobatics","Animal Handling","Arcana","Athletics","Deception","History","Insight","Intimidation","Investigation","Medicine","Nature","Perception","Performance","Persuasion","Religion","Sleight of Hand","Stealth","Survival"],"title":"skill proficiency"},{"k":"tl","t":"tool","n":1,"cats":["art","music","game","other"],"title":"Tool proficiency"}]},"Green-Skin":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Natural armor of 13 + Dex, Advantage against Poisoned, and Poison Resistance.","full":"Your people feed on sunlight through tough, photosynthetic skin.\n**Natural Armor.** While you wear no armor, your base Armor Class is 13 plus your Dexterity modifier. You can use a Shield and keep this benefit.\n**Photosynthetic Resilience.** You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Poisoned condition.\n**Poison Resistance.** You have Resistance to Poison damage.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"res":["Poison"],"notes":[["Advantage","Saves to avoid or end Poisoned (Green-Skin)"],["Note","Green-Skin: with no armor, AC = 13 + Dex (Shield allowed)"]]}},"Grue":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Re-hide as a Reaction, Darkvision 120 feet, and self-cast Invisibility in dim light or darkness from level 5.","full":"One of your parents was a creature of darkness, such as a shadow. Your skin is black, and you cast a shadow in every direction, even in bright light. In shadows you are nearly invisible.\n**Covert.** When you are hidden and a creature finds you with a successful Wisdom (Perception) check, you can take the Hide action as a Reaction. If your Dexterity (Stealth) roll beats that creature's Wisdom (Perception) check, you silently move and it does not notice you. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Darkvision.** You have Darkvision with a range of 120 feet.\n**Swirl of Shadows.** From character level 5, you can cast Invisibility on yourself without a spell slot while you are entirely in Dim Light or Darkness. The spell ends early if you have the Incapacitated condition or end your turn in Bright Light. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"senses":[["Darkvision",120,""]]}},"Gun-Mage Adept":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Dex. Martial ranged weapon proficiency, Finger Guns, and Firearm spells always prepared up to your Proficiency Bonus.","full":"Raise Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Ranged Weapon Proficiency.** You gain proficiency with Ranged Martial weapons.\n**Cantrip.** You learn the Finger Guns cantrip.\n**Expanded Spell List.** Spells with the Firearm tag join your spell list.\n**Spells Prepared.** Choose a number of Firearm spells equal to your Proficiency Bonus. They are always prepared for you. When you gain a level, you can swap one of them for a different Firearm spell.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["DEX"],"fx":{"notes":[["Proficiency","Ranged Martial weapons (Gun-Mage Adept)"]]}},"Hacker":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Int. Data proficiency or Expertise, a built-in Interface Rig, hacking as a Utilize action, and hacking from 60 feet.","full":"Raise Intelligence by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Black Hat.** You are always treated as having an Interface Rig. Devices also never lock after your hacking attempts.\n**Data Expert.** You gain proficiency in the Data skill. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it.\n**Quick Hack.** You can try to hack a device with the Utilize action instead of over one minute.\n**Ranged Hack.** You can try to hack Magical Technology you can see within 60 feet of you.","pre":"Level 4+, Int 13+","asi":["INT"],"fx":{"notes":[["Proficiency","Data, or Expertise in it if already proficient (Hacker)"]]}},"Heavy Gunner":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Str. Use Strength for Heavy or Two-Handed ranged weapons, and knock a target Prone on a ranged Critical Hit.","full":"Raise Strength by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Strong Attacks.** You can use Strength instead of Dexterity for attack and damage rolls with Ranged weapons that have the Heavy or Two-Handed property.\n**Enhanced Critical.** Right after you score a Critical Hit with a Ranged weapon, you can give the target the Prone condition.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+","asi":["STR"]},"Inventor":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+1 Int. Learn two Gadgeteer Gadgets with no prerequisite, swap one on each level, and use 8 + Int + Proficiency as the save DC.","full":"Raise Intelligence by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Gadgets.** You gain two Gadgets of your choice from the Gadget Options of the Gadgeteer class. They cannot have a prerequisite, and the Magic Item Gadget is not allowed. When you gain a level, you can swap one of your Gadgets for another one you qualify for. No other creature can use your Gadgets. If you lose one, you can replace it when you finish a Long Rest. If a Gadget requires a saving throw, the DC is 8 plus your Intelligence modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus.","pre":"Level 4+, Int 13+","asi":["INT"]},"Artillerist (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Use the mastery of two ship weapon kinds you are proficient with, and ship weapon attacks crit on 19 or 20.","full":"**Ship Weapon Mastery.** You can use the mastery property of two kinds of ship weapons of your choice, provided you are proficient with them. When you finish a Long Rest, you can change which two kinds.\n**Expanded Critical.** Your attack rolls with ship weapons score a Critical Hit on a 19 or 20 on the d20.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it."},"Industrious":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Origin feat. A d6 on failed checks with a chosen skill, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest, and Advantage against Exhaustion.","full":"**Hardworking.** Choose one skill you are proficient in. Each time you gain a level, you can pick a different skill to replace it. When you fail an ability check with that skill, you can roll a d6 and add it to the roll, which may turn the failure into a success. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses when you finish a Long Rest.\n**Strong Core.** You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid the Exhaustion condition.","fx":{"notes":[["Advantage","Saves to avoid Exhaustion (Industrious)"]]}},"Insectoid":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Species feat for Near-Humans. Blindsight 10 feet and regrowth of lost body parts in 24 hours.","full":"You have a few insect features, such as compound eyes or chitinous plates, and almost always a pair of sensitive antennae.\n**Blindsight.** Your antennae give you Blindsight with a range of 10 feet.\n**Regenerative.** If a body part is amputated and the loss does not kill you, it fully regrows within 24 hours.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"senses":[["Blindsight",10,""]]}},"Intrepid Captain":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. A second Captain action as a Bonus Action, crew Immunity to Frightened, and Persuasion proficiency or Expertise.","full":"**All Hands on Deck.** When you take an action from the Captain Crew Role, you can take another action from that role as a Bonus Action. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Dauntless Command.** While you are the Captain, the ship's crew have Immunity to the Frightened condition.\n**Galactic Diplomat.** You gain proficiency in Persuasion. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it.\n**Ship Feat.** Ship feats match the Crew Roles aboard a starship. The DM can grant one to confirm your role or to reward good work in it.","fx":{"skills":["Persuasion"],"notes":[["Proficiency","Expertise in Persuasion if already proficient (Intrepid Captain)"]]}},"Iron Hero":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"+2 AC against attackers with CR above your level. Advantage against foes that downed an ally. Reaction to stop a Legendary Action, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Underdog's Resolve.** When a creature whose CR is higher than your level attacks you, you gain a +2 bonus to AC against that attack.\n**Vengeful Strike.** You have Advantage on attack rolls against a creature that has dropped one of your allies to 0 Hit Points since the end of your last turn.\n**Heroic Intervention.** When an enemy you can see takes a Legendary Action, you can use your Reaction to step in and stop that action from happening. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Ironwood Dryad":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Without armor, AC is 15 (a Shield is allowed). Magic action: spend a Hit Die to heal, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"**Barkflesh.** While you wear no armor, your AC is 15. You can carry a Shield and keep this benefit.\n**Natural Regeneration.** As a Magic action you can mend your wooden flesh. Spend one Hit Point Die, roll it, and regain Hit Points equal to the roll plus your Constitution modifier. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Elf","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Barkflesh: AC 15 with no armor, a Shield is allowed (Ironwood Dryad)"]]}},"Jinx":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"When you roll a 1 on a D20 Test, a creature within 60 feet has Disadvantage on its next D20 Test. An enemy's natural 13 against you or your spell save becomes a 1.","full":"**Mutual Misery.** When you roll a 1 on the d20 for a D20 Test, pick a creature you can see within 60 feet. For the next minute, it has Disadvantage on the next D20 Test it makes.\n**Unlucky Number.** When an enemy rolls a 13 on the d20 for an attack against you, or for a saving throw against a spell you cast, the roll counts as a 1."},"Lakshay: Oni":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Advantage on Piloting a Battleframe and on Intimidation and Persuasion with those who know your rank. Add Proficiency Bonus to a damage roll, save or AC once per turn.","full":"Joining Lakshay normally grants the Ship feat Battleframe Dragoon in place of a Faction feat. You earn the rank of Oni only after proving yourself as a Dragoon.\n**Battleframe Expertise.** You have Advantage on Dexterity (Piloting) checks made while piloting a Battleframe.\n**Fearsome Reputation.** When you take the Influence action against a creature that knows your rank of Oni, you have Advantage on Charisma (Intimidation and Persuasion) checks.\n**Oni's Skill.** You can add your Proficiency Bonus to one damage roll or saving throw you make, or to your AC against one attack that hits you, which may turn the hit into a miss. After you do this, you cannot do it again until the start of your next turn.","pre":"Battleframe Dragoon feat, 100 confirmed kills"},"Laser Swordsmaster":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Crits with laser blades add maximum damage instead of doubling dice. Reaction: add Proficiency Bonus to AC against a blaster hit and maybe deflect it.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Cauterizing Critical.** When you score a Critical Hit with an Antimatter Dagger, Laser Claws, Laser Sword or Laser Greatsword, you slash through the target. Instead of rolling the damage dice twice, you add the maximum damage of the attack to the roll.\n**Deflect Blaster.** While you hold one of those four weapons and a creature hits you with a ranged blaster attack, you can use your Reaction to add your Proficiency Bonus to your AC against that attack. If that makes it miss, you can bounce the bolt at a creature you can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw (DC 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus the modifier of the ability this feat raised) or take the damage the triggering attack would have dealt.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+ and Dex 13+","asi":["STR","DEX"]},"Latent Psionics":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Empathy as a Magic action. Psionic Blast deals an extra 1d10 Psychic damage. Mage Hand cantrip with an Invisible hand.","full":"**Empathy.** As a Magic action, you can probe the mind of a creature you can see within 30 feet and learn its emotional state.\n**Improved Psionic Blast.** Your Psionic Blast deals an extra 1d10 Psychic damage.\n**Minor Kinesis.** You learn the Mage Hand cantrip, and the hand is Invisible when you cast it this way. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it (choose when you take this feat).","pre":"Wrothian"},"Leviathan Suit":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Integrate one weapon, or two without the Two-Handed property, into your Aqua Suit. Blindsight 10 feet in the suit, 30 feet underwater.","full":"**Integrated Weapons.** You can build one weapon into your Aqua Suit, or two weapons (one in each arm) if neither has the Two-Handed property. A weapon you draw from the suit snaps into your hand and you cannot be disarmed of it. You can change which weapons are integrated when you finish a Long Rest.\n**Sonar.** While you wear your Aqua Suit, you have Blindsight out to 10 feet, or 30 feet when you are underwater.","pre":"Nautilid","fx":{"senses":[["Blindsight",10,"Leviathan Suit","30 feet underwater, only while wearing your Aqua Suit"]]}},"Lilliputian":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Your size is Tiny. Your weapon damage dice drop one step. Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage.","full":"You belong to a rare line of halflings who are as small next to normal halflings as those are next to humans.\n**Tiny.** Your size is Tiny.\n**Miniature Weapons.** You can only wield weapons made for your size. They match the standard versions but their damage dice drop one step (d12 or 2d6 becomes d10, then d8, then d6, then d4, with d4 as the minimum).\n**Nimble.** Opportunity Attacks have Disadvantage against you.","pre":"Halfling","fx":{"notes":[["Note","Lilliputian: size is Tiny, weapon damage dice drop one step, Opportunity Attacks against you have Disadvantage"]]}},"Magitechnician (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Your magic items use a better save DC when higher. Recharge one item on a Short Rest as if dawn had come, once per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Magic Item Expert.** If one of your magic items calls for a saving throw, it uses this DC when it is higher: 8 plus the modifier of the ability this feat raised plus your Proficiency Bonus.\n**Magic Item Recharge.** When you finish a Short Rest, you can make one magic item that regains charges or properties recharge as if the next dawn had come. After you do this, finish a Long Rest to do it again.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Marksman's Luck":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Once per turn flip one damage die on a Ranged weapon hit (not a d4). A ranged Critical Hit sets the target's Speed to 0 until the end of its next turn.","full":"Raise Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Flip Die.** Once per turn, when you roll damage with a Ranged weapon, you can turn one of the damage dice over and use the number on its underside. This does not work on d4s. On a balanced die, the top and bottom numbers add up to one more than the highest face.\n**Enhanced Critical.** When you score a Critical Hit with a Ranged weapon, the target's Speed is 0 until the end of its next turn.","pre":"Level 4+, Dex 13+","asi":["DEX"]},"Mechanic":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Technology proficiency (Expertise if you have it). Overheat on any blaster with extra damage of twice Proficiency Bonus. Mending, and Greater Mending once per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Burn Out.** You can use the Overheat mastery property on any blaster, even without Weapon Mastery, and it does not count against your mastery weapon limit. When you use it through this feat, the extra damage equals twice your Proficiency Bonus and the weapon stays Overheated until you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest.\n**Technology Expert.** You gain proficiency in Technology. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it instead.\n**Vent Tape Repairs.** You can cast Mending by using up a negligible amount of Vent Tape. By using up a whole roll of Vent Tape, you can cast Greater Mending once with no spell slot. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for these spells. After you cast Greater Mending this way, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Level 4+, Int 13+","asi":["INT"],"fx":{"skills":["Technology"]}},"Merc":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Swap a blaster's mastery for Bludgeon. Heavy or Two-Handed ranged hits within 10 feet add Proficiency Bonus damage. Learn Common Sign Language.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Blaster Melee.** When you attack with a blaster, you can swap its mastery property for Bludgeon on that attack. You can use Bludgeon with the blaster even without Weapon Mastery, and it does not count against your mastery weapon limit.\n**Point Blank.** When you hit a creature within 10 feet with a ranged attack using a weapon with the Heavy or Two-Handed property, the target takes extra damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus, of the same type the weapon deals.\n**Tactical Signals.** You learn Common Sign Language. You can send a tactical message of 10 words or fewer to a creature that can see you signal. It need not share a language with you, but it must understand at least one language.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+ and Dex 13+","asi":["STR","DEX"],"fx":{"langs":["Common Sign Language"]}},"Metabolistic Magic (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"After failing a D20 Test, spend a spell slot to add 2 plus its level. On a Short Rest spend Hit Dice to regain slots, once per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Arcane Skill.** When you fail a D20 Test, you can spend a spell slot to add a bonus to the roll, which can turn it into a success. The bonus is 2 plus the level of the slot.\n**Vital Fuel.** When you finish a Short Rest, you can spend Hit Point Dice up to your Proficiency Bonus to regain spell slots. Choose slots whose combined level is no more than the number of Hit Dice spent. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Level 4+, Spellcasting","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Multiscale":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Pick a second Draconic Ancestry. Resistance to both damage types and either one for your Breath Weapon. Breath Weapon deals an extra 1d10.","full":"**Dual Ancestry.** Pick a second Draconic Ancestry option. Your scales show both dragon ancestors. You have Resistance to the damage type of each ancestry and can use either type for your Breath Weapon.\n**Improved Breath Weapon.** Your Breath Weapon deals an extra 1d10 damage of the type set by your Draconic Ancestry.","pre":"Dragonborn"},"Night Blessed":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Stealth proficiency. Reaction to Hide when found, once per Rest. Reaction to move 5 feet without Opportunity Attacks when an enemy misses you in melee.","full":"You were born in tune with shadow rather than the sun.\n**Covert.** When you are hidden and a creature finds you with a successful Wisdom (Perception) check, you can use your Reaction to take the Hide action. If your Dexterity (Stealth) roll beats that Perception check, you slip to a new spot unseen and the creature does not notice you. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Craven.** When an enemy you can see misses you with a Melee attack, you can use your Reaction to move 5 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks.\n**Stealthy.** You gain proficiency in Stealth.","pre":"Avia-Ra","fx":{"skills":["Stealth"]}},"Porterling":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Advantage to escape grapples and nonmagical restraints. Move through the space of larger creatures. Add a d8 to High and Long jumps.","full":"You have a human parent and a gnome or halfling parent. You stand about as tall as a dwarf but are leaner, and you cannot grow a thick beard.\n**Flexible.** You have Advantage on checks to end the Grappled condition or to escape nonmagical restraints.\n**Nimbleness.** You can move through the space of any creature one size larger than you, but you cannot stop there.\n**Springheel Leap.** When you make a High Jump or Long Jump, you can roll a d8 and add the result in feet to the distance, even on a standing jump. Each foot still costs a foot of movement.","pre":"Near-Human"},"Precognitive":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Augury always prepared and free once per Long Rest. At the start of your turn, record a d20 to swap in for any D20 Test, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Augury.** You always have Augury prepared. You can cast it with no spell slot and no components, and then you need a Long Rest before casting it that way again. You can also cast it with spell slots. Your spellcasting ability for it is the ability this feat raised.\n**Impressions of the Future.** At the start of your turn, you can roll a d20 and record the number. Before the start of your next turn, you can use it in place of the roll of any D20 Test made by you or by a creature you can see. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Proto-Man":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Advantage on saves against the Frightened condition. Hit Point maximum rises by 1, and by 1 again each level.","full":"You come from a world of ancient animals and huge plants. Your people are tough and sturdy, much like early humans.\n**Brave.** You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end the Frightened condition.\n**Primal Toughness.** Your Hit Point maximum increases by 1, and it increases by 1 again each time you gain a level.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"notes":[["Advantage","Saves to avoid or end Frightened (Brave)"]]}},"Psionic-Awakened":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Empathy as a Magic action. Mage Hand with extra range, Invisible hand and no V or S components. Unseen Servant at level 3 and Levitate at level 5, each free once per Long Rest.","full":"Most humans hold a faint psionic potential. You have unlocked yours, which may show as stark white hair, glowing pupils, or hair and clothes that drift about you.\n**Empathy.** As a Magic action, you can probe the mind of a creature you can see within 30 feet and learn its emotional state.\n**Psionics.** You learn the Mage Hand cantrip. You can cast it without Verbal or Somatic components, make the hand Invisible, and its range increases by 30 feet. At character level 3 you learn Unseen Servant, and at character level 5 you learn Levitate. You always have them prepared. You can cast each once without a spell slot and regain that ability when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast them with spell slots. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for them (choose when you take this feat).","pre":"Near-Human"},"Two-Headed":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Advantage on Initiative once per Rest. Advantage on saves against Blinded, Charmed, Deafened and Frightened. You stay conscious during a Long Rest.","full":"Like an ettin, you have two heads with different personalities sharing one body.\n**Look Both Ways.** You can have Advantage when you roll Initiative. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again.\n**Two Heads.** You have Advantage on saving throws to avoid or end these conditions: Blinded, Charmed, Deafened and Frightened.\n**Wakeful.** One head is always awake, so you stay conscious during a Long Rest.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"notes":[["Advantage","Saves to avoid or end Blinded, Charmed, Deafened, Frightened (Two Heads)"]]}},"Reanimated":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"You are Undead. No Exhaustion from lacking food, drink or air. Scare a creature within 30 feet at Initiative. Resistance to Necrotic damage.","full":"You hover between death and life. You might be a classic undead such as a revenant, or the product of reckless science or a magical accident.\n**Creature Type.** You are Undead.\n**Deathless Body.** Going without food, drink or air does not give you levels of Exhaustion.\n**Scare.** When you roll Initiative, you can pick a creature you can see within 30 feet. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus) or have the Frightened condition until the end of its turn.\n**Undead Resistances.** You have Resistance to Necrotic damage.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"res":["Necrotic"]}},"Pyromaniac (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Fire Bolt. Burning Hands and Scorching Ray prepared, each free once per Long Rest. Reroll maximum Fire damage dice up to your Proficiency Bonus.","full":"Raise Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Firestarter Magic.** You know Fire Bolt and always have Burning Hands and Scorching Ray prepared. You can cast each of those two spells once without a slot, and need a Long Rest to do so again. You can also cast them with slots. The spellcasting ability is the one this feat raised.\n**Flare Damage.** When you deal Fire damage and roll the highest number on a damage die, you can roll that die again and add it, and keep rolling while you get the highest number. You can add at most a number of dice equal to your Proficiency Bonus (minimum 1).","pre":"Level 4+","asi":["INT","WIS","CHA"]},"Reptiloid":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Acid Spit replaces an attack: 60 feet, 1d10 Acid, scaling at levels 5, 11 and 17. Resistance to Acid, Fire or Poison.","full":"You have scaly, rough skin, slit eyes and a forked tongue.\n**Acid Spit.** When you take the Attack action, you can replace one attack with a spat glob of acid. It is a ranged attack with a range of 60 feet, you are proficient with it, and you add your Dexterity modifier to its attack and damage rolls. On a hit the target takes 1d10 Acid damage. This becomes 2d10 at character level 5, 3d10 at level 11 and 4d10 at level 17. You can use it a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.\n**Reptilian Resistance.** You have Resistance to Acid, Fire or Poison damage (choose when you take this feat).","pre":"Near-Human"},"Roguean":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Darkvision 60 feet. Resistance to Cold damage. No damage from cold Extreme Temperatures.","full":"You come from an icy, barren world flung away from its sun by some disaster. Surviving there gave you these traits.\n**Darkvision.** You have Darkvision out to 60 feet.\n**Cold Resistance.** You have Resistance to Cold damage.\n**Extremophile.** You take no damage from cold Extreme Temperatures. Extreme heat affects you as normal.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"res":["Cold"],"senses":[["Darkvision",60,""]]}},"S.S. St. Vincent: Archon":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Medicine proficiency and Spare the Dying as a Bonus Action. Reaction: Advantage on D20 Tests after an enemy Bloodies you or an ally, once per Long Rest.","full":"You stand as a beacon of law and order on the Frontier.\n**First Aid.** You gain proficiency in Medicine. You also learn the Spare the Dying cantrip and can cast it as a Bonus Action.\n**White Angel's Vengeance.** When an enemy you can see within 60 feet deals damage that makes you or an ally you can see within 60 feet Bloodied, you can use your Reaction to gain Advantage on D20 Tests until the end of your next turn. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","fx":{"skills":["Medicine"]}},"Scale and Fang: Scaleguard":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Bonus Action: an ally within 5 feet uses your AC if it is higher, until your next turn. Don or doff a Shield as a Bonus Action.","full":"As a bodyguard of Scale & Fang, your duty is to protect your charge at any cost.\n**Block.** As a Bonus Action, pick an ally you can see. Until the start of your next turn, while that ally is within 5 feet of you, its AC equals your AC if yours is higher. The effect ends early if you or the ally become Incapacitated.\n**Quick Shield.** You can don or doff a Shield as a Bonus Action."},"Sepulcher Knight: Deputy":{"weapons":"Repeater","cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. A badge that sways attitudes, Manacles as a Bonus Action, and a service Repeater you are proficient with, including its mastery.","full":"You have been sworn in as a deputy or trainee of a Knight's Precinct, which gives you a badge and a gun.\n**Badge.** You can show your badge on your turn with no action. Creatures that see it treat you as they would the Sepulcher Knights. Law-abiding citizens are often Friendly and criminals are often Hostile.\n**Cuffs.** You can use Manacles as a Bonus Action.\n**Gun.** You are issued a Repeater as your service weapon. You are proficient with it and can use its mastery property even without Weapon Mastery, and it does not count against your mastery weapon limit."},"Shapeshifter":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Spend 1 minute to change your appearance to anything of your size and basic shape, including another species. Your statistics stay the same.","full":"Using your Biomimicry trait over 1 minute, you can fully reshape your look. You choose height, weight, facial features, voice, hair length, coloring and other details. You can pass as a member of another species, though none of your statistics change. You cannot look like a creature of a different size, and your basic shape stays the same.","pre":"Amoeboid"},"Shock Trooper (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"When you roll Initiative without Disadvantage, draw a weapon and attack. Your Speed doubles in the first round of combat.","full":"Raise Strength or Dexterity by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**First Strike.** When you roll Initiative and do not have Disadvantage on the roll, you can draw a weapon and make an attack with it.\n**Rapid Advance.** In the first round of each combat, your Speed is doubled.","pre":"Level 4+, Str 13+ and Dex 13+","asi":["STR","DEX"],"fx":{"notes":[["Note","Shock Trooper: first combat round Speed is doubled. On Initiative you can draw a weapon and attack"]]}},"Showman (Dark Matter)":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Performance proficiency (Expertise if you have it). Bonus Action taunt: Disadvantage on a creature's next attack against others. Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"Raise Charisma by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n**Expert Performer.** You gain proficiency in Performance. If you already have it, you gain Expertise in it instead.\n**Taunt.** As a Bonus Action you can mock a creature within 15 feet. If it can hear you (it need not understand), it has Disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes against a creature other than you before the end of its next turn. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Level 4+, Cha 13+","asi":["CHA"],"fx":{}},"Silver-Tongued":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Use Int, Wis or Cha for Persuasion. Influence can raise a Hostile creature to Indifferent or an Indifferent one to Friendly. Learn three languages.","full":"**Argumentative.** You can use Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma for Persuasion checks.\n**Diplomatic.** When you take the Influence action, you can treat a Hostile creature as Indifferent, or an Indifferent creature as Friendly.\n**Polyglot.** You learn three languages of your choice."},"Simian":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Climb Speed equal to your Speed. A prehensile tail that holds objects but cannot attack. Reaction to cut fall damage by five times Proficiency Bonus.","full":"Your people evolved along a different path from High Terra and look like monkeys or apes. You are as clever as anyone else, you just like bananas a bit more.\n**Climbing Speed.** You have a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.\n**Prehensile Tail.** You can hold and use objects and weapons with your hands, feet and tail, but you cannot make attacks with a weapon held by your tail.\n**Soft Landing.** When you fall, you can use your Reaction to reduce the fall damage by five times your Proficiency Bonus.","pre":"Near-Human","fx":{"notes":[["Speed","Climb Speed equal to your Speed (Simian)"]]}},"Technical":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Build a device that casts a non-damaging Wizard cantrip, changeable each Long Rest. Use Intelligence for one skill's checks and swap the skill each level.","full":"**Cantrip Device.** You build a device that lets you cast one cantrip of your choice from the Wizard list that deals no damage (choose when you build it). When you finish a Long Rest, you can build a new device with a different cantrip, and the old one stops working. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it (choose when you take this feat).\n**Mind Over Matter.** Pick one skill. When you make an ability check with that skill, you can use your Intelligence modifier in place of the normal ability modifier. Each time you gain a level, you swap that skill for a different one."},"Technopath":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Technomancy cantrip. Technical Difficulties at level 3 and Circuit Breaker at level 5, each free once per Long Rest.","full":"You know the Technomancy cantrip. At character level 3 you learn Technical Difficulties, and at character level 5 you learn Circuit Breaker. You always have these spells prepared. You can cast each once without a spell slot and regain that ability when you finish a Long Rest. You can also cast them with spell slots. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for them (choose when you take this feat).","pre":"Gnome"},"The Cabal: Soul Broker":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Gain Soul Credits equal to the CR of enemies you kill (10 credits trade for 100 CR). Advantage on Influence against Hostile creatures, once per Rest.","full":"You have passed the legal and ritual exams to become a bonded soul broker for the Cabal.\n**Soul Dividends.** You are paid for sending souls onward. When you kill an enemy, you gain 1 Soul Credit for each point of its Challenge Rating, rounded down (minimum 0). You can trade 10 Soul Credits for 100 CR.\n**Moral Relativism.** When you make an Influence check against a Hostile creature, you can have Advantage on the roll instead of Disadvantage. After you use this, finish a Short Rest or Long Rest to do so again."},"The Coalition: Recruit":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Gain Athletics, Martial weapons, Light armor or Shield training. Reaction to move 15 feet after a Dexterity save against an area effect, once per Long Rest.","full":"To join the Coalition you went through hard training or achieved a feat that stands for it.\n**Basic Training.** You gain one of these, your choice: proficiency in Athletics, proficiency with Martial weapons, training with Light armor, or training with Shields. If you already have all of them, you gain Weapon Mastery with the Repeater or Standard Carbine instead, and it does not count against your mastery weapon limit.\n**Dive for Cover.** When you make a Dexterity saving throw against an effect with an area, you can use your Reaction to move up to 15 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks, which may take you out of the area. After you do this, finish a Long Rest to do so again."},"The Firm: Contractor":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Simple weapons that deal 1d4 deal 2d4 instead. Expertise in one skill you know.","full":"You are a licensed Contractor. The pen may beat the sword, but the dagger beats them both.\n**Backstabber.** When you hit a creature with a Simple weapon that deals 1d4 damage, it deals 2d4 damage instead.\n**Expertise.** You gain Expertise in one skill you are proficient in, your choice."},"The Tower: Agent":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Faction feat. Illusory Script free with Intelligence. Cast spells without V, S or non-costly M components, Proficiency Bonus times per Long Rest.","full":"As a full Tower Agent you know the organization's secret ciphers and its quiet magical arts.\n**Mark of Induction.** You bear a tattoo that only other Tower Agents can see, marking your membership.\n**Mage Cypher.** You can cast Illusory Script without a spell slot or Material components. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for it.\n**Subtle Spell.** When you cast a spell, you can cast it without Verbal, Somatic or Material components, except Material components the spell consumes or that have a stated cost. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses on a Long Rest.","pre":"Spellcasting"},"Upgraded":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Reconfigure Ability Scores as a Bonus Action, once per Long Rest. Magic action to swap Thermalsight for Blindsight 10 feet or Darkvision 120 feet.","full":"**Configuration Upgrade.** You can use your Reconfigurable Ability Scores as a Bonus Action, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a Long Rest.\n**Improved Optics.** As a Magic action, you can swap your Thermalsight for Blindsight with a range of 10 feet or Darkvision with a range of 120 feet. The sense lasts until you use this feature again to go back to Thermalsight or pick a different one.","pre":"Vect"},"Versatile Passenger":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Ship feat. Help the Engineer (ship regains Shield Points equal to Proficiency Bonus), the Gunner (Advantage on attacks) or the Pilot (Advantage on the ship's saves).","full":"You may have no fixed Crew Role, but you know how to be useful in a crisis.\n**Engineer Helper.** You can take the Help action to assist the Engineer. The ship regains Shield Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and other ships have Disadvantage on saving throws against this ship's systems until the start of your next turn.\n**Gunner Helper.** You can take the Help action to assist the Gunner. The Gunner has Advantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn.\n**Pilot Helper.** You can take the Help action to assist the Pilot. The Pilot has Advantage on saving throws made on behalf of the ship until the start of your next turn."},"Warzone Nomad":{"cat":"G","hb":"DM24","d":"Dash as a Bonus Action and gain Temporary Hit Points equal to Proficiency Bonus. Drop to 1 Hit Point instead of 0 once per Long Rest.","full":"**Adrenaline Rush.** You can take the Dash action as a Bonus Action. When you do, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses when you finish a Short Rest or Long Rest.\n**Relentless Endurance.** When you are reduced to 0 Hit Points but not killed outright, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead. After you use this, finish a Long Rest to do so again.","pre":"Orc"}};
var FTLU=[{"src":"feat","owner":"Arcane Cannoneer","feature":"Arcane Cannoneer","n":"Over-Cast","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Astrogations Inc.: Starguide","feature":"Astrogations Inc.: Starguide","n":"Momentary Prescience","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Battleframe Dragoon","feature":"Battleframe Dragoon","n":"Relentless Retaliation","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Clown","feature":"Clown","n":"Pratfall","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Church of the Sun Above: Adherent","feature":"Church of the Sun Above: Adherent","n":"Solar Judgement","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Creative","feature":"Creative","n":"Innovation","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Cyberfiend","feature":"Cyberfiend","n":"Translocator","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"short","tag":"Bonus Action"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Dogfighter","feature":"Dogfighter","n":"Barrel Roll","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Exomorph","feature":"Exomorph","n":"Molt","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Bonus Action"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Grafter","feature":"Grafter","n":"Machine Precision","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Grue","feature":"Grue","n":"Covert","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Industrious","feature":"Industrious","n":"Hardworking","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Intrepid Captain","feature":"Intrepid Captain","n":"All Hands on Deck","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":""},{"src":"feat","owner":"Iron Hero","feature":"Iron Hero","n":"Heroic Intervention","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Ironwood Dryad","feature":"Ironwood Dryad","n":"Natural Regeneration","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Magic action"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Magitechnician (Dark Matter)","feature":"Magitechnician (Dark Matter)","n":"Magic Item Recharge","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Short Rest"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Mechanic","feature":"Mechanic","n":"Greater Mending (Vent Tape)","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Full roll of Vent Tape"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Metabolistic Magic (Dark Matter)","feature":"Metabolistic Magic (Dark Matter)","n":"Vital Fuel","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Short Rest"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Night Blessed","feature":"Night Blessed","n":"Covert","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Precognitive","feature":"Precognitive","n":"Impressions of the Future","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Start of turn"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Two-Headed","feature":"Two-Headed","n":"Look Both Ways","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Initiative"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Reptiloid","feature":"Reptiloid","n":"Acid Spit","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Replaces an attack"},{"src":"feat","owner":"S.S. St. Vincent: Archon","feature":"S.S. St. Vincent: Archon","n":"White Angel's Vengeance","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Showman (Dark Matter)","feature":"Showman (Dark Matter)","n":"Taunt","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Bonus Action"},{"src":"feat","owner":"The Cabal: Soul Broker","feature":"The Cabal: Soul Broker","n":"Moral Relativism","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"short","tag":"Influence check"},{"src":"feat","owner":"The Coalition: Recruit","feature":"The Coalition: Recruit","n":"Dive for Cover","lvl":1,"max":1,"reset":"long","tag":"Reaction"},{"src":"feat","owner":"The Tower: Agent","feature":"The Tower: Agent","n":"Subtle Spell","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"long","tag":"Cast without components"},{"src":"feat","owner":"Warzone Nomad","feature":"Warzone Nomad","n":"Adrenaline Rush","lvl":1,"max":"pb","reset":"short","tag":"Bonus Action"}];
