var SPR=[["Antimatter Mine",4,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Until dispelled",0,0,"DEX","Range 6,000 ft. A mine (AC 15, 10 Mega HP) detonates when a ship or Mega creature comes within 1,000 ft. Dexterity save, 4d12 Necrotic to Mega targets (half on success). +1 mine per slot level above 4.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Antivirus",1,"Abjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S","24 hours",0,1,"","Touch, 24 hours. A device cannot be disabled by magic, infected by the N-Virus or inhabited by an AI. Hackers have Disadvantage on Intelligence (Data) checks against it.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Astrogation",7,"Divination",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Burn rare spices (100+ CR, consumed) to plot a course. A void jump made before it ends is an assisted jump.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Autopilot",1,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","1 hour",0,1,"","Touch, 1 hour. A spaceship flies itself toward a known destination by the safest route. It rolls its own saves if no Pilot, adding your spellcasting modifier. 8 hours with a level 3+ slot.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Awaken Machine",6,"Transmutation",["Bard","Druid","Witch","Wizard"],"8 hours","Touch","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Touch, 8 hours casting. Install a diamond Construct core (1,000+ CR, consumed) in a Construct with Charisma 3 or less or Magical Technology. It gains Charisma 10, Intelligence 10 if lower, and speech.","DM24",["Bard","Druid","Witch","Wizard"]],["Circuit Breaker",2,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Reaction","Self (5 ft emanation)","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"DEX","Reaction when a creature you see within 5 ft damages you. 5-ft Emanation, Dexterity save, 3d8 Lightning (half on success). Disables nearby Magical Technology. +1d8 per slot level above 2.","DM24",["Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Commandeer Ship",3,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. Wisdom save or a Fighter-size ship comes under your control. It repeats the save when damaged. Bigger ships with higher slots.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Conjure Asteroid",1,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 hour. Summon an asteroid of radius up to 1,500 ft (AC 15, 100 Mega HP). +1 asteroid per slot level above 1.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Conjure Shuttle",5,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Investigator","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"10 minutes","100 ft","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Range 100 ft, 10 minutes casting, 1 hour. A holographic Shuttle appears (Fly 100 ft in atmosphere). Reaches space in 5 minutes of vertical flight. Ends at 0 Mega HP or on recast.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Investigator","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Create Vacuum",4,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft-radius Sphere with no air. Gases there are destroyed. A creature without a breathing apparatus that ends its turn inside suffocates and gains 1 Exhaustion.","DM24",["Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Dark Matter Override",5,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"WIS","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 hour. A Frigate or smaller ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail its Speed and Maneuverability are 0 until the end of its next turn, then it saves again or makes a blind void jump.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Digitize",6,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Touch. You and up to 8 willing creatures linking hands around an Arcane Terminal or computer move to Cyberspace, or back to the Material Plane. Natives of Cyberspace arrive in hardlight bodies.","DM24",["Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Disable Weapon",1,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail one weapon you choose is disabled, and you can switch which one as a Magic action. It repeats the save each turn.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Ear Worm",1,"Enchantment",["Bard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Wisdom save or the target loses Concentration, is Deafened, and cannot concentrate while it lasts.","DM24",["Bard"]],["Eldritch Rift",4,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","9000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 9,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 1,500-ft Sphere of tentacled portals is Difficult Terrain. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 3d6 Mega Bludgeoning and have Speed 0.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Electromagical Pulse",4,"Evocation",["Bard","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self (30 ft emanation)","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Self (30-ft Emanation), concentration 1 minute. Magical Technology in the area is disabled. Constructs make a Constitution save or are Incapacitated with Speed 0, repeating each turn.","DM24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Failsafe Spellhack",1,"Abjuration",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action right after a slotted spell fails to affect any creature. You recover the slot you spent. You can cast it and another slotted spell on the same turn.","DM24",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Geodesic Shield",2,"Conjuration",["Martyr","Paladin","Ranger"],"Action","60 ft","V, S","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Range 60 ft, concentration 10 minutes. A 15-ft Emanation of force plates (AC 10, 20 HP) holds breathable air, blocks gas and ranged attacks, and insulates against Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums. +1 AC and +10 HP per slot level above 2.","DM24",["Martyr","Paladin","Ranger"]],["Greater Mending",3,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","120 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Range 120 ft. Fully repair an object up to 10 ft in any dimension, including a broken magic item. Restores 6d8 + spellcasting modifier Mega HP to a ship.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Hack System",2,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"WIS","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 10 minutes. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail one system you choose is disabled and cannot be repaired. It repeats the save each turn.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Battleframe",5,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","1000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Range 1,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. Summon a hardlight Battleframe and teleport into its Pilot seat. Its Escape Pod lasts 1 hour after the spell ends. Uses the slot level in the stat block.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Blaster",1,"Conjuration",["Bard","Necromancer","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","10 ft","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Range 10 ft. A hovering blaster fires at a target within 60 ft of it. Ranged spell attack, 3d6 Force. It can use its own line of sight. +1d6 per slot level above 1.","DM24",["Bard","Necromancer","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Chains",1,"Conjuration",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"STR","Range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Strength save or Restrained. The target can use an action for a Strength (Athletics) check against your save DC to break free. +1 target per slot level above 1.","DM24",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Construction",3,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","30 ft","V, S, M","10 minutes",0,0,"","Range 30 ft, 10 minutes. Build a Huge or smaller hardlight object (15-ft Cube) with no moving parts. AC 12, HP 30 + spellcasting modifier. +10 HP per slot level above 3.","DM24",["Cleric","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Frame",5,"Conjuration",["Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Up to 10 minutes",1,0,"","Self, concentration 10 minutes. Power armor: Large size, AC 17, 10 Temporary HP at the start of each turn, Advantage on Strength checks and saves, two battlefists (melee spell attack, 2d8 + modifier Force, reach 10 ft), Extra Attack.","DM24",["Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Gauntlet",3,"Evocation",["Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Touch. Three melee spell attacks on one target: first hit 1d12, second 2d12, third 3d12 Force. A level 5-6 slot adds a fourth attack (4d12), level 7+ adds a fifth (5d12).","DM24",["Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Object",0,"Conjuration",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warmage","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Self, 1 hour. Create a hardlight copy of a Bell, Chain, Crowbar, Flask, Grappling Hook, Iron Spikes (10), Rope, Sack, Signal Whistle or Shovel. It sheds Dim Light in 5 ft. Up to three at a time.","DM24",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warmage","Wizard"]],["Hardlight Trap",2,"Conjuration",["Necromancer","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","120 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 120 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft Cube of hidden traps. On casting and as a Bonus Action later, creatures you choose make a Dexterity save or take 2d6 Force (half on success). +1d6 per slot level above 2.","DM24",["Necromancer","Ranger","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Imitation Spellhack",2,"Evocation",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Reaction","60 ft","V, S","1 hour",0,0,"","Reaction when a creature within 60 ft casts a spell with V, S or M components of a level you can cast. You memorize it for 1 hour. It ends after you cast it.","DM24",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Improvised Spellhack",5,"Evocation",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action when you cast a spell with a slot of level 5 or lower. Swap it for any spell on your list of the same level with an action casting time, even if unprepared.","DM24",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Ionize",7,"Transmutation",["Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","150 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 150 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 20-ft-radius Sphere of plasma, Heavily Obscured. Dexterity save, 10d6 Fire (half on success), rising by 2d6 each of your turns up to 20d6. Entering or ending a turn there forces the save.","DM24",["Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Local Jump",2,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Self. Teleport your ship up to 3,000 ft in any direction and turn it to face any way.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Meteoroid Shower",2,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A 2,000-ft Cube of micro-meteors is Difficult Terrain. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 2d4 Mega Bludgeoning (half on success).","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Mutate",6,"Transmutation",["Druid","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","10 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"CON","Range 10 ft, concentration 1 hour. A Large or smaller Beast or familiar makes a Constitution save or becomes a Mutant (Avian, Cephalopod or Insectoid) and gains Temporary HP equal to the form's HP. It is your ally.","DM24",["Druid","Necromancer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Orbital Hardlight Cannon",9,"Conjuration",["Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Action","500 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 500 ft, concentration 1 minute. A beam in a 15-ft-radius, 1-mile-high Cylinder. Dexterity save, 12d8 Radiant (half on success). Move it 60 ft with a Magic action. Ignites loose flammables.","DM24",["Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Overcharge Weapon",2,"Enchantment",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Self, concentration 1 minute. One installed ship weapon deals an extra 1d6 Force damage on a hit.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Phase Shift",3,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Self, concentration 1 minute. Your ship goes partly ethereal. Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage to it is reduced by your spellcasting modifier. It moves through creatures and objects as Difficult Terrain and takes 5 (1d10) Mega Force if it ends a turn inside one.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Ray Spellhack",1,"Evocation",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action when you cast an instantaneous spell that needs a save. Turn it into a ray at one target within 120 ft. Ranged spell attack. On a hit it auto-fails the save. Legendary Resistance can turn the hit into a miss.","DM24",["Bard","Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Recharge Shields",1,"Abjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Self. Your ship regains all of its Shield Points.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Sequenced Spellhack",4,"Evocation",["Sorcerer","Wizard"],"10 minutes","Self","V, S, M","8 hours",0,0,"","Self, 10 minutes casting, 8 hours. Cast three level 1-2 action spells now without effect, then release all three with one Magic action later. A level 6+ slot allows two level 3 spells, or levels 3, 2 and 1.","DM24",["Sorcerer","Wizard"]],["Shield Burst",3,"Evocation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self (3000 ft emanation)","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"DEX","Range 3,000-ft Emanation, concentration 1 minute. Fails if your ship has no Shield Points. When your ship loses all Shield Points, it erupts. Mega targets make a Dexterity save or take 5d8 Lightning (half on success).","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Shield Disruption",4,"Abjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self (1500 ft emanation)","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Self (1,500-ft Emanation), concentration 1 minute. Ships in the area lose their Shield Points and cannot regain them while inside.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Simulation",5,"Divination",["Cleric","Druid","Wizard"],"10 minutes","Self","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Self, 10 minutes casting. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. The GM summarizes the likely events of the next 24 hours, ignoring things you do not know or unlikely events.","DM24",["Cleric","Druid","Wizard"]],["Speedcycle",4,"Conjuration",["Bard","Martyr","Paladin","Ranger","Wizard"],"Action","Touch","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"DEX","Touch, concentration 1 hour. A force motorcycle (AC 15, 40 HP, seats two) appears. Mount or dismount once per turn for half your Speed. Bonus Actions: Bail (6d6 Fire blast), Driveby (40 ft, Advantage and +1d8 on a melee attack), Floor It (100 ft).","DM24",["Bard","Martyr","Paladin","Ranger","Wizard"]],["Splice",4,"Transmutation",["Druid","Necromancer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Range 60 ft, 1 hour. Take genetic material from a creature (alive or dead within 10 days) and give a recipient within 5 ft one of its traits plus its Speeds, Resistances or special senses. The GM picks the trait.","DM24",["Druid","Necromancer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Summon Hardlight Spirit",4,"Conjuration",["Wizard"],"Action","90 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,0,"","Range 90 ft, concentration 1 hour. A hardlight Construct appears in a free space you can see and uses the Hardlight Spirit stat block. It vanishes at 0 HP or when the spell ends.","DM24",["Wizard"]],["Technical Difficulties",1,"Transmutation",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","60 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"","Bonus Action, range 60 ft, concentration 1 minute. Pick a piece of Magical Technology in range. It malfunctions and is disabled for the duration.","DM24",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Technomancy",0,"Transmutation",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Warmage","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Cantrip, range 60 ft. Perform a basic operation on a device you see, such as pressing a button, typing about a dozen keystrokes, or an authorized action. You cannot rewire it or bypass authorization without a Hacking attempt.","DM24",["Bard","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Warmage","Witch","Wizard"]],["Transfer Consciousness",8,"Necromancy",["Cleric","Necromancer","Wizard"],"1 hour","Touch","V, S, M","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Touch, 1 hour casting. Needs a gold-plated cable (1,000+ CR) and a vect Construct body (2,000+ CR) or a computer. Move a willing or Unconscious creature's soul into a Construct body, or back up a digital imprint of it.","DM24",["Cleric","Necromancer","Wizard"]],["Transferred Spellhack",3,"Transmutation",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","30 ft","V, S","8 hours",0,0,"","Bonus Action when you cast an action spell with a level 1-3 slot. Give it to a willing creature within 30 ft instead. It casts it as a Reaction, free of slot and Material components, using your DC and attack bonus, and keeps it prepared for 8 hours.","DM24",["Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["Turbulence",1,"Transmutation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","6000 ft","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"WIS","Range 6,000 ft, concentration 1 minute. A ship makes a Wisdom save. On a fail its Speed is halved and its Maneuverability drops to 45 degrees if higher.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Upgraded Spellhack",1,"Evocation",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"],"Bonus Action","Self","V, S","Instantaneous",0,0,"","Bonus Action when you cast a spell with a slot. Raise the spell's effective level by 1, to a maximum of 9. You can cast it and another slotted spell on the same turn.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Witch","Wizard"]],["White Dwarf",8,"Conjuration",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"],"Action","1 mile","V, S, M","Up to 1 minute",1,0,"CON","Range 1 mile, concentration 1 minute. An artificial star (10-ft-radius Sphere) with 60-ft heat and 15-ft extreme heat Emanations. Constitution save: 4d8 Radiant (8d8 in extreme heat), pulled 10 ft toward it, half damage on success. Touching it deals 8d8.","DM24",["Cleric","Druid","Sorcerer","Warlock","Wizard"]],["Worldseek",1,"Divination",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","Self","V, S, M","Up to 1 hour",1,1,"","Self, concentration 1 hour. You know the direction and distance to the nearest planet, planetoid or moon. Fails if you are already on one.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Martyr","Necromancer","Paladin","Ranger","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]],["Zone of Atmosphere",2,"Conjuration",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"],"Action","60 ft","V, S, M","1 hour",0,0,"","Range 60 ft, 1 hour. A 30-ft-radius Sphere of clean breathable air, or a 30-ft Emanation around an unattended object. Gas and smoke cannot enter. Insulates against Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums.","DM24",["Bard","Cleric","Druid","Investigator","Necromancer","Sorcerer","Warlock","Witch","Wizard"]]];
var SPF={"Antimatter Mine":"Range 6,000 ft, until dispelled. You place an explosive anti-ship mine at a point you choose in range. It has AC 15, 10 Mega Hit Points and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. Reducing it to 0 Hit Points sets it off, which can chain into nearby mines.\n\n**Detonation.** The mine explodes in a 1,000-foot Emanation if a ship or Mega creature comes within 1,000 feet of it or ends its turn there. Each Mega target in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 4d12 Necrotic damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You create one more mine for each slot level above 4.","Antivirus":"Touch, 24 hours. You ward a device against digital intruders. For the duration it cannot be disabled by magical effects such as Technical Difficulties or Electromagical Pulse, cannot be infected by the N-Virus, and cannot be inhabited by an AI or similar creature. If a creature already inhabits it, that creature is pushed out into a free space within 5 feet of the device. Creatures also have Disadvantage on Intelligence (Data) checks made to hack the device.","Astrogation":"Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: rare spices and incense worth 100+ CR, which the spell consumes. By burning them you work out your path through the universe. If you make a void jump before the spell ends, it counts as an assisted jump.","Autopilot":"Touch, 1 hour. You give a spaceship a limited ability to run without its crew. Name a destination the ship knows, such as the nearest Maw station or a planet. At the start of the Initiative order the ship moves toward it by the safest route. This movement pauses while a creature holds the Pilot Crew Role. If the ship has no Pilot, it makes saving throws for itself and adds your spellcasting ability modifier to them.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 3 or higher slot the duration is 8 hours.","Awaken Machine":"Touch, instantaneous, casting time 8 hours. Material: a diamond Construct core worth 1,000+ CR, which the spell consumes. You fit an upgraded core into a Construct with a Charisma of 3 or less, or into a piece of Magical Technology. The target gains Charisma 10, Intelligence 10 if it was lower, and the ability to speak one language you know. The GM picks fitting statistics, such as a Single-Task Automaton or a Hardlight Avatar. The awakened machine is Friendly toward you and your allies, or Indifferent if you or your allies have ever damaged it.","Circuit Breaker":"Reaction, taken when a creature you can see within 5 feet of you damages you. Self (5-foot Emanation). You release a burst of electricity. Each creature in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 3d8 Lightning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. Magical Technology in the area is disabled until the end of your next turn. Items you wear or carry are not affected.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 2.","Commandeer Ship":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. One Fighter-size ship you can see in range makes a Wisdom save. On a fail you commandeer it for the duration. Whenever it takes damage it repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success. While you share a plane with it you override its flight controls. On its turn you can use your Reaction to dictate how it moves and what it attacks. If you do not, it acts as it likes.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** A level 5 or 6 slot lets you target a Personal ship. A level 7 or 8 slot lets you target a Transport. A level 9 slot lets you target a Corvette.","Conjure Asteroid":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 hour, concentration. You summon a spherical asteroid in an empty space of your choice in range. You choose its radius, up to 1,500 feet. It is an object with AC 15 and 100 Mega Hit Points, and it has Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You summon one more asteroid for each slot level above 1.","Conjure Shuttle":"Range 100 feet, 1 hour, casting time 10 minutes. Material: a starship's launch button. A Shuttle (see the Ships chapter) with glowing holographic circuits appears in range. In atmosphere it has a Fly Speed of 100 feet. It reaches space after 5 minutes of flying straight up on most planets, and enters an atmosphere by descending for the same time. The spell ends early if the Shuttle drops to 0 Mega Hit Points or you cast the spell again. When it ends, the Shuttle sinks gently to the ground if a planetoid is close, giving passengers time to leave.","Create Vacuum":"Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a bit of kindling. You create a Sphere of 20-foot radius with no air, centered on a point in range. Airborne substances such as poison gas, smoke or fog cannot enter, and any already inside are destroyed. A substance made by a spell of higher level than this one is unaffected.\n\nA creature with no breathing apparatus that ends its turn in the Sphere begins suffocating and gains 1 Exhaustion level. When that creature can breathe again, it removes every Exhaustion level it gained this way.","Dark Matter Override":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a dial with eleven levels. You try to force a Frigate or smaller ship you can see in range into a blind void jump. The ship makes a Wisdom save. A ship without a Dark Matter engine able to jump passes automatically. On a fail, the ship's Speed and Maneuverability are 0 until the end of its next turn, and then it must save again. If it fails the second save, it at once makes a blind void jump.","Digitize":"Touch, instantaneous. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You and up to 8 willing creatures who link hands around the computer are carried to Cyberspace, the plane of neon and data that lies inside connected planetary networks. The spell can also carry you and up to 8 willing creatures who link hands from Cyberspace back to the Material Plane. A creature native to Cyberspace, such as an Artificial Intelligence, that arrives on the Material Plane has a body of hardlight. The GM picks fitting statistics, such as a Hardlight Avatar.","Disable Weapon":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a cork stopper. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, one of its installed weapons that you choose is disabled for the duration. On later turns you can use a Magic action to change which weapon is disabled. At the end of each of its turns the ship repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success.","Ear Worm":"Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. You hum a catchy tune to a creature you can see in range. The target makes a Wisdom save. On a fail it loses Concentration on any spell or effect and has the Deafened condition until the spell ends. While Deafened this way, it cannot maintain Concentration on anything.","Eldritch Rift":"Range 9,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a pickled tentacle. You open many portals to an eldritch dimension in a 1,500-foot Sphere centered on a point in range. Alien tentacles reaching from the portals make the Sphere Difficult Terrain for the duration. Each Mega target in it makes a Dexterity save. On a fail the target takes 3d6 Mega Bludgeoning damage and has Speed 0 until the spell ends or it takes the Dodge or Evasive Maneuvers action. A target also makes the save when it enters the area or ends its turn there, but only once per turn.","Electromagical Pulse":"30-foot Emanation from you, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a bit of frayed wire. With a clap you release a wave of energy. Magical Technology in the area is disabled for the duration. A creature can take the Utilize action to reboot a piece of Magical Technology within reach.\n\nEach Construct in the area makes a Constitution save. On a fail it has the Incapacitated condition and its Speed is 0 for the duration. An Incapacitated Construct repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.","Failsafe Spellhack":"Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken right after you cast a spell with a spell slot that fails to affect any creature. You recover the slot you spent on that spell. This only works if the spell affected no one, for example it dealt no damage, every spell attack missed, or every target passed its save and suffered no effect. The GM decides whether the triggering spell qualifies. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn.","Geodesic Shield":"Range 60 feet, 10 minutes, concentration. Clear triangular plates of force form a 15-foot Emanation that starts on you or on a point you choose in range. The area holds clean, breathable air, and poison gas, smoke and fog cannot enter. It insulates those inside from Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums. Creatures can walk in and out freely, but the barrier blocks ranged attacks, spells and other effects. It has AC 10 and 20 Hit Points. The spell ends early if it is reduced to 0 Hit Points.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Its AC rises by 1 and its Hit Points by 10 for each slot level above 2.","Greater Mending":"Range 120 feet, instantaneous. Material: two lodestones. You repair breaks, tears and other damage on an object you can see in range, such as a smashed control panel, torn radiation plating, a ruined keycard or a jammed turbine. If the object is no larger than 10 feet in any dimension, you mend it with no trace of the damage and return it to working order. A broken magic item can be repaired if its magic was present when it broke, but lost charges do not return. The spell can also mend a damaged ship, restoring Mega Hit Points equal to 6d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier.","Hack System":"Range 6,000 feet, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: a bit of frayed wire. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, one of its systems that you choose is disabled and cannot be repaired for the duration. At the end of each of its turns the ship repeats the save and the spell ends on it on a success.","Hardlight Battleframe":"Range 1,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR and a plastic figurine. You call a Battleframe made of hardlight into an empty space you can see in range and teleport into its Pilot seat. It uses the Hardlight Battleframe stat block. The Battleframe vanishes when it drops to 0 Mega Hit Points or the spell ends, but its Escape Pod stays for 1 hour after the spell ends.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell's level in the stat block.","Hardlight Blaster":"Range 10 feet, instantaneous. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You conjure a blaster of compressed light that hovers within 10 feet of you and fires a beam at a target you choose within 60 feet of it. Make a ranged spell attack. The blaster is the origin point of the attack, so it can hit a creature outside your line of sight as long as the blaster can see it. On a hit the target takes 3d6 Force damage. The blaster then fades.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 1.","Hardlight Chains":"Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You weave light into chains and try to bind a creature you can see in range. The target makes a Strength save or has the Restrained condition for the duration. A Restrained creature can use an action to make a Strength (Athletics) check against your spell save DC. On a success it breaks free and is no longer Restrained by the chains.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** You can target one more creature for each slot level above 1.","Hardlight Construction":"Range 30 feet, 10 minutes. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You compress light into a solid structure in range. It can be Huge or smaller, fitting in a 15-foot Cube (27 joined 5-foot cubes), such as a bridge over a chasm, a tower above the trees or a patch for a ship's hull. It has no moving parts and cannot directly harm anyone. Whatever you build has AC 12 and Hit Points equal to 30 + your spellcasting ability modifier. If it reaches 0 Hit Points it collapses and the spell ends. On your turn you can dismiss it as a free action.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The object has 10 more Hit Points for each slot level above 3. With a level 6 or higher slot you can use a Magic action to change it into another object that fits the limits. This does not restore its Hit Points.","Hardlight Frame":"Self, 10 minutes, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. Plates of compressed light cover your body as power armor. For the duration:\n\n**Size.** You become Large if you were smaller.\n\n**Hardlight Armor.** Your AC is 17 and your Dexterity modifier does not change it. You can use a Shield with it.\n\n**Temporary Hit Points.** You gain 10 Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of your turns.\n\n**Mighty.** Advantage on Strength checks and saving throws.\n\n**Integrated Battlefists.** You are proficient with the two battlefists. Attack with them using a melee spell attack against a target within 10 feet. A hit deals Force damage equal to 2d8 + your spellcasting ability modifier.\n\n**Extra Attack.** You attack twice instead of once when you take the Attack action.","Hardlight Gauntlet":"Touch, instantaneous. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You conjure a gauntlet of energy and unleash a flurry. Make three melee spell attacks against one target. The first hit deals 1d12 Force damage, the second hit 2d12, and the third hit 3d12.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 5 or 6 slot you make four attacks, and the fourth hit deals 4d12 Force damage. With a level 7 or higher slot you make five attacks, and the fifth hit deals 5d12 Force damage.","Hardlight Object":"Self, 1 hour. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You press light into the shape of one of these objects: Bell, Chain, Crowbar, Flask, Grappling Hook, Iron Spikes (10), Rope, Sack, Signal Whistle or Shovel. The object sheds Dim Light in a 5-foot radius and lasts for the duration. If you cast the spell several times, you can keep up to three hardlight objects at once. You can dismiss one on your turn as a free action.","Hardlight Trap":"Range 120 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You lay hidden hardlight traps across a 20-foot Cube in range. When you cast the spell, and as a Bonus Action on each of your later turns, you can set off spikes, swinging pendulums, buzzsaws and the like inside the Cube. Each creature you choose in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 2d6 Force damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** The damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2.","Imitation Spellhack":"Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Casting time: Reaction, taken when you see a creature within 60 feet of you cast a spell that has Verbal, Somatic or Material components and is of a level you can cast. You memorize that spell for a while. For the duration you have it prepared. This spellhack ends after you cast the prepared spell.","Improvised Spellhack":"Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot of level 5 or lower. You replace that spell with any spell on your spell list that is of the same level and has a casting time of an action. You do not need to have it prepared. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn.","Ionize":"Range 150 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a matchbox. You heat the air in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered on a point in range until it turns to plasma. The area is Heavily Obscured. When the Sphere appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity save and takes 10d6 Fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A creature also makes the save when it enters the Sphere for the first time on its turn or ends its turn there, but only once per turn. The damage rises by 2d6 at the start of each of your turns, to a maximum of 20d6.","Local Jump":"Self, instantaneous. You teleport your ship up to 3,000 feet in any direction and turn it to face whichever way you choose.","Meteoroid Shower":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. You call down a rain of tiny meteors in a 2,000-foot Cube, which is Difficult Terrain for the duration. Each Mega target in the Cube makes a Dexterity save and takes 2d4 Mega Bludgeoning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. A target also makes the save when it enters the Cube or ends its turn there, but only once per turn.","Mutate":"Range 10 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a sample of radium. You scramble the genes of a Large or smaller Beast or familiar in range. It makes a Constitution save or twists into a hulking abomination. Its statistics are replaced by the Mutant stat block, though it keeps its Hit Points. When you cast the spell, choose Avian, Cephalopod or Insectoid. The target gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the Mutant form, and the spell ends on it early when those are gone.\n\nThe creature is an ally to you and your allies. In combat it shares your Initiative count and acts right after you. It obeys your spoken commands (no action from you). If you give none, it takes the Dodge action and moves to avoid danger.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** Use the slot's level as the spell's level in the stat block.","Orbital Hardlight Cannon":"Range 500 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You shape light into a huge construct, an orbital cannon 1 mile above your head. It fires a blinding beam into a Cylinder of 15-foot radius and 1-mile height centered on a point in range. When the Cylinder appears, each creature in it makes a Dexterity save and takes 12d8 Radiant damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. The beam ignites flammable nonmagical objects in the area that nobody wears or carries.\n\nOn later turns you can use a Magic action to move the Cylinder up to 60 feet. A creature also makes the save when the Cylinder moves into its space and when it enters the area or ends its turn there. A creature makes this save only once per turn.","Overcharge Weapon":"Self, 1 minute, concentration. Choose one weapon installed on your ship. Until the spell ends, attacks with that weapon deal an extra 1d6 Force damage on a hit.","Phase Shift":"Self, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a flawless crystal. Your ship shifts between planes and becomes partly ethereal. Whenever an attack hits it, the Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage it takes is reduced by your spellcasting ability modifier. The ship can also move through creatures and objects as if they were Difficult Terrain. It takes 5 (1d10) Mega Force damage if it ends its turn inside a creature or object.","Ray Spellhack":"Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast an instantaneous spell that requires a saving throw. Instead of its normal area, you channel the spell into a ray at one target. Make a ranged spell attack against a target within 120 feet of you. On a hit, the target is affected by the spell and automatically fails its save against it. A creature with Legendary Resistance can use it to make this attack miss instead. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn.","Recharge Shields":"Self, instantaneous. Material: a bubble wand. Your ship regains all of its Shield Points.","Sequenced Spellhack":"Self, 8 hours, casting time 10 minutes. Material: a spell sequencer worth 5,000+ CR. Choose three different level 1 or 2 spells you can cast that have a casting time of an action. You cast all three now, each with the lowest slot possible and in any order. They do not take effect yet. These are the sequenced spells. Before the spellhack ends you can take a Magic action to cast them in the order you first cast them. All three count as part of that one Magic action and use components as normal. You cannot cast another spell with a spell slot on the same turn. You choose targets for the sequenced spells as each is cast. The spellhack then ends. Casting it again ends the effect of an earlier Sequenced Spellhack on you.\n\n**Higher-Level Spell Slot.** With a level 6 or higher slot you can sequence two level 3 spells, or one each of level 3, level 2 and level 1.","Shield Burst":"3,000-foot Emanation from your ship, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a handful of glass shards. You charge your ship's shields with crackling energy. The spell fails if the ship has no Shield Points when you cast it. When the ship loses all of its Shield Points, energy erupts in a 3,000-foot Emanation and the spell ends. Each Mega target in the area makes a Dexterity save and takes 5d8 Lightning damage on a fail, or half as much on a success.","Shield Disruption":"1,500-foot Emanation from your ship, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a needle. Your ship sends out a frequency that breaks shields. A ship in the area loses its Shield Points and cannot regain them until it leaves the area.","Simulation":"Self, instantaneous, casting time 10 minutes. Material: an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You run a detailed digital simulation of the next day's events and gain insight into a likely future. The GM gives you a summary of what probably happens in the next 24 hours. You set the parameters from what you know, so the summary leaves out unknown facts (an ambush waiting for you, a traitor among you) and unlikely events (gaining or losing a companion).","Speedcycle":"Touch, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a set of keys. A Medium motorcycle of magical force appears under a creature you touch. You choose its look, but it always has two wheels and seats two Medium or Small creatures. You or a creature you choose can operate it, using at least one hand at all times, and one creature can ride along. A creature can mount or dismount once per turn, spending movement equal to half its Speed (round down). The motorcycle is an object with AC 15 and 40 Hit Points. At 0 Hit Points it coasts to a stop and fades, giving rider and passenger time to dismount, and the spell ends.\n\nWhile you operate it you can use a Bonus Action for one of these:\n\n**Bail.** You and the passenger leap off and are Prone. The motorcycle speeds up to 60 feet in a direction you choose and explodes in a 10-foot-radius Sphere on the first Medium or larger obstacle it hits. Each creature there makes a Dexterity save and takes 6d6 Fire damage on a fail, or half as much on a success. The spell then ends.\n\n**Driveby.** The motorcycle moves up to 40 feet without provoking Opportunity Attacks. You can split this movement across your turn. If you make a melee attack during it, you have Advantage on the roll and deal an extra 1d8 damage of the attack's type on a hit.\n\n**Floor It.** The motorcycle moves up to 100 feet. If it provokes an Opportunity Attack while you ride it, the attacker can target you or the motorcycle. With this Bonus Action it can travel 30 miles in an hour, or up to 80 miles on an open paved road.","Splice":"Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Material: a glass syringe worth 1,000+ CR. A thin beam of arcane energy takes a genetic sample from a creature you can see in range and gives it to a recipient within 5 feet of you. The donor does not need to be alive if you target a part of a creature that died within the last 10 days. The recipient gains one of the donor's traits, such as a ghast's Stench or a dwarf's Stonecunning, and also one of these: the donor's Speeds, Resistances or special senses. The GM chooses which trait, if any, is gained. Only traits and statistics native to the donor can pass over, not spells or gear affecting it. The recipient looks like a mix of the donor and itself. The changes and the gained statistics last for the duration.","Summon Hardlight Spirit":"Range 90 feet, 1 hour, concentration. Material: an emerald ring worth 30+ CR. You call forth a hardlight Construct of gleaming gears, pistons, plates and motors. It appears in an empty space you can see in range and uses the Hardlight Spirit stat block. It vanishes when it drops to 0 Hit Points or when the spell ends.","Technical Difficulties":"Range 60 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Casting time: Bonus Action. Material: a bit of frayed wire. Lights flicker, blasters jam and Arcane Terminals crash. Choose a piece of Magical Technology in range. It malfunctions unpredictably and is disabled for the duration.","Technomancy":"Range 60 feet, instantaneous. With a complex gesture you manipulate a technological device you can see in range. You can do any basic operation on it, including pressing an external button, entering about a dozen keystrokes, doing an authorized operation (such as opening an unlocked door), dimming or brightening a screen, or muting a noisy device. You cannot disconnect or reconnect wires, and you cannot do an unauthorized operation without making a Hacking attempt.","Transfer Consciousness":"Touch, instantaneous, casting time 1 hour. Material: a gold-plated cable worth 1,000+ CR, plus either a Construct body made of vect components worth 2,000+ CR or an Arcane Terminal or similar computer. You move the soul of a willing creature, or one that has the Unconscious condition, into a machine. When you cast it, choose one option.\n\n**Transfer Soul.** The soul moves from its body into a waiting Construct body. The target controls the new body if its soul is free to do so, and keeps its memories of its past life and its capabilities. It swaps its species for vect and changes its traits to match. Its old body falls into an indefinite catatonic state.\n\n**Backup Soul.** A digital imprint of the target's soul, with its personality and experiences, is uploaded to an Arcane Terminal or similar computer such as a ship's computer. If the target dies, its soul moves to the terminal, provided the soul is free and willing to return. If a waiting Construct body is linked to the terminal, the soul moves into it automatically as in Transfer Soul, and the backup is erased. The creature recalls only what it knew up to the moment you cast this spell.","Transferred Spellhack":"Range 30 feet, 8 hours. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot of level 1 to 3 that has a casting time of an action. Instead of the spell taking effect, you hand it to a willing creature in range. That creature can at once take a Reaction to cast it, with no spell slot and no Material components, using your spell save DC and spell attack modifier. If the spell needs Concentration, the target maintains it. The target also has the spell prepared for the duration and can cast it with its own spell slots of the right level, using its own spellcasting ability. It loses the prepared spell if you cast this spellhack again. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn.","Turbulence":"Range 6,000 feet, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a fan. Pick a ship you can see in range. It makes a Wisdom save. On a fail, its Speed is halved and its Maneuverability is lowered to 45 degrees if it was higher, for the duration.","Upgraded Spellhack":"Self, instantaneous. Casting time: Bonus Action, taken when you cast a spell with a spell slot. The triggering spell's effective level rises by 1, up to a maximum of level 9. You can cast this spellhack and another spell with a spell slot on the same turn.","White Dwarf":"Range 1 mile, 1 minute, concentration. Material: a pair of spectacles made from darkened glass. You create an artificial star, a brilliant 10-foot-radius Sphere in an empty space you can see in range. It makes a 60-foot Emanation of heat and a 15-foot Emanation of extreme heat. Whenever a creature enters either Emanation or ends its turn there, it makes a Constitution save. On a fail it takes 4d8 Radiant damage (8d8 if it is in the extreme heat Emanation) and is pulled 10 feet straight toward the star. On a success it takes half damage and is not pulled. A creature or object that touches the star's Sphere takes 8d8 Radiant damage.\n\nThe Sphere gives Bright Light in a 1-mile radius and Dim Light for 1 more mile. If any of its area overlaps an area of Darkness made by a spell of level 8 or lower, that spell is dispelled.","Worldseek":"Self, 1 hour, concentration. Material: a spyglass. The spell shows the way to the nearest planet. For the duration you know the direction and distance to the nearest planet, planetoid or moon. If you cast it while standing on a planet, planetoid or moon, the spell fails.","Zone of Atmosphere":"Range 60 feet, 1 hour. Material: a glass fish bowl. You make a 30-foot-radius Sphere of clean, breathable air centered on a point you can see in range. You can instead cast it on an object that nobody wears or carries, so the air fills a 30-foot Emanation from that object. Poison gas, smoke and fog cannot enter the area, and any already inside are destroyed. A substance made by a spell of higher level than this one is unaffected. The area insulates those inside from Extreme Temperatures and Vacuums."};
var IT=[["Additional Arms","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 450 gp). A second pair of working arms fitted below the first. They can hold weapons and a Shield (two Two-Handed weapons, or four one-handed ones), and can make Somatic components and other actions. They give no extra actions and no extra graft slots.",{}],["Android Skin","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (External slot, 8,000 gp). Mechanical skin and muscle that make you look exactly human. Your other grafts cannot be seen while it is installed. Each skin copies a real person, living or dead.",{}],["Arcane Resonator","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 5,500 gp). Lets you attune to up to four magic items at once.",{}],["Cantrip Module","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot, 250 gp). It is loaded with one cantrip from the Cleric, Druid or Wizard list, chosen when it is made. While it is installed you know that cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma is its spellcasting ability, chosen each time you install the graft.",{}],["Arm Blade","Weapon","Common",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 400 gp). A wide blade that replaces an arm. It cannot be taken from you by disarming. It has no hand, so you cannot hold a weapon, Shield or other object in that arm. Martial Melee weapon, 1d10 Slashing, Finesse, Slow mastery.",{"wp":{"d":"1d10","t":"Slashing","cat":"M","k":"M","p":"Finesse","m":"Slow","w":0,"xw":1},"base":["Arm Blade"]}],["Arm Cannon","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 800 gp). A strong blaster cannon that replaces an arm. It cannot be taken from you by disarming. It has no hand, so you cannot hold a weapon, Shield or other object in that arm. Martial Ranged weapon, 2d8 Radiant, range 30/120, Blaster, Firearm and Recoil, Push mastery.",{"wp":{"d":"2d8","t":"Radiant","cat":"M","k":"R","p":"","m":"Push","w":0,"xw":1,"r":"30/120"},"base":["Arm Cannon"]}],["Black Box","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot, 500 gp). Records everything you see and hear while it is installed, so you recall it with perfect clarity. It survives otherwise catastrophic damage to your body. A DC 15 Intelligence (Technology) check recovers its memories, and a failure corrupts the data for good. The data is also corrupted if the box is installed in a new host. The memories can be played on a Datapad, Arcane Terminal or similar computer, or uploaded to a new body or a Personality Module with the Transfer Consciousness spell.",{}],["Climbing Apparatus","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Legs slot, 500 gp). A device that lets you cling to surfaces and move well on walls and ceilings. You gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. It may look like extra limbs, magnetic pads or a grappling launcher.",{"fx":{"climb":"walk"}}],["Clockwork Wings","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"Graft (External slot, 40,000 gp). Silver mechanical wings folded into your back. They give you a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. Deploy or retract them as a Bonus Action. You can also deploy them as a Reaction while you fall.",{"fx":{"fly":"walk"}}],["Concentration Module","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 850 gp). A second mechanical mind that helps you hold your focus. When you make a Constitution saving throw to keep Concentration on a spell, you can add your Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma modifier instead of your Constitution modifier. You choose which when you install the graft.",{}],["Embedded Armor","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (External slot, 700 gp). Your base AC is 13 plus your Dexterity modifier. You can wear armor over it and use whichever gives the better AC. You can use a Shield and keep this benefit.",{"fx":{"acBase":13}}],["Ankh of Ra","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A golden holy symbol that shields you from death. If you drop to 0 Hit Points while wearing it, roll 4d10 and your Hit Points become that number instead. The ankh then loses its luster and becomes nonmagical. **Magic Item Set.** Attuning to this ankh, a Heretical Sunstaff of Ra and Solar Wings of Ra counts as attuning to one item. While you are attuned to the ankh and one of those items, the ankh does not become nonmagical. It instead goes dull until the next dawn and cannot be used again before then.",{}],["Arcane Terminal","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A 500-lb computer with a keyboard and monitor. **Data Storage.** It stores any amount of text, images and video. An authorized user can search its data and that of any linked terminal as a Utilize action. Terminals on settled worlds are often joined in planetary nets, while a lone terminal usually holds only a few subjects. **Communication Network.** With an installed antenna, authorized users can connect to it with a Datapad out to 1 mile and talk by text, audio or video. **Ship Computers.** A starship usually has one to run its sensors and systems. Terminals can also open doors in a facility, give orders to Constructs, or process technical data. **Hacking.** Access is normally limited to authorized users. A DC 15 Intelligence (Data) check hacks a terminal. Safer systems can have higher DCs.",{}],["Arcane Warhead","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"A 4,000-lb bomb. **Arming.** Over 1 minute, you can arm it if you know its command code and hold a key made for it. Then choose Timed or Impact detonation. Timed sets a delay of 1 minute, 10 minutes or 1 hour. Impact leaves it dormant until it is reduced to 0 Hit Points. It has AC 18, 100 Hit Points (1 Mega Hit Point) and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage. **Detonation.** Within a 10-mile-radius Sphere, each creature and object takes 10d10 + 200 Mega Radiant damage. Each creature outside it but within a 100-mile-radius Sphere makes a DC 20 Dexterity save and takes 10d10 + 50 Radiant damage on a fail or half on a success. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity. A creature damaged by it is Poisoned for 24 hours. The center of the blast becomes a spherical Dead Magic Zone from a few dozen feet to several miles across.",{}],["Attractor Mine","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A small metal disk humming with gravity (50 gp). When you take the Attack action, you can swap one attack for throwing it at a space you see within 30 ft. It sticks firmly to any surface it touches. A creature other than you that enters the 5-ft Cube above it or starts its turn there makes a DC 13 Strength save or has its Speed reduced to 0 until the start of its next turn. After 10 minutes the mine burns out and becomes nonmagical.",{}],["B.E.G.","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"An experimental weapon of unmatched power. As a Magic action, set off an explosion of lightning and plasma in a 30-ft-radius Sphere centered on a point you see within 120 ft. Each creature in it makes a DC 18 Dexterity save and takes 10d10 + 50 Radiant damage on a fail or half on a success. Once used, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Ballistic Sledge","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A Rocket Hammer (2d6 Bludgeoning, Heavy, Two-Handed, Cleave mastery). Once on each of your turns when you make a melee attack with it, you can fire its thrusters. You first lunge up to 15 ft toward the target, which costs no movement and provokes no Opportunity Attacks. A hit deals an extra 1d4 Bludgeoning damage. **Upgraded Magic Item.** At character level 5 you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, rising to +2 at level 11 and +3 at level 17.",{"base":["Rocket Hammer"]}],["Blaster Mod (+1 Enchanted Battery)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An arcane battery that hums with magic. While installed, you have a +1 bonus to ranged attack and damage rolls with this blaster, which counts as a magic weapon. The bonus depends on the battery's rarity and does not stack with a magic weapon that already has a bonus to attack and damage rolls.",{}],["Blaster Mod (+2 Enchanted Battery)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"An arcane battery that hums with magic. While installed, you have a +2 bonus to ranged attack and damage rolls with this blaster, which counts as a magic weapon. The bonus depends on the battery's rarity and does not stack with a magic weapon that already has a bonus to attack and damage rolls.",{}],["Blaster Mod (+3 Enchanted Battery)","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"An arcane battery that hums with magic. While installed, you have a +3 bonus to ranged attack and damage rolls with this blaster, which counts as a magic weapon. The bonus depends on the battery's rarity and does not stack with a magic weapon that already has a bonus to attack and damage rolls.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Aimbot)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A mod with a built-in Construct that corrects your aim. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. When you make a ranged attack with this blaster, you can spend 1 charge to let the Aimbot attack for you. You skip rolling the d20 and count it as a 10. With Advantage or Disadvantage, the 10 replaces only one of the two dice and you roll the other normally.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Blaster Mod (Antimatter Battery)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"While installed, this blaster deals Necrotic damage instead of its normal type. The target's Hit Points maximum drops by the Necrotic damage it takes. It dies if that maximum reaches 0.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Beam Module)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A module on the barrel. When you make a ranged attack with this blaster, you can focus the shot into a 5-ft-wide Line out to the weapon's normal range. Each creature in it makes a DC 13 Dexterity save. On a fail it takes the weapon's normal damage plus 2d6 Radiant, or half as much on a success. The blaster then Overheats and cannot attack again until the end of your next turn. Once used, the mod cannot be used again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Blaster Mod (Dragonfire Break)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"While this barrel attachment is installed, the blaster deals Fire damage instead of its normal type and adds 1d6 Fire damage to any target it hits.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Electrocoil)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A barrel module that sparks into the aperture. While installed, the blaster deals Lightning damage instead of its normal type and gains the Jolt mastery in addition to its own. You can use only one mastery per attack. You can use its Jolt even without the Weapon Mastery feature, and it does not count against the number of weapons you can use.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Extended Barrel)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"The blaster's normal and long ranges double.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Magnetic Mount)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A quantum electromagnet on the blaster. As a Bonus Action, you can pull the blaster to your free hand if it is within 60 ft of you and no one carries it. You cannot be disarmed of it unless you are Incapacitated.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Overcharge Module)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An external battery that overloads the blaster. When you make a ranged attack with it, you can fire an overcharged shot that deals an extra 6d6 damage on a hit. The blaster then Overheats and cannot attack again until the end of your next turn. Once used, the mod cannot be used again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Blaster Mod (Reinforced Frame)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A composite alloy frame that guards the blaster against impacts and lets you use it as a club. The weapon gains the Bludgeon mastery in addition to its own. You can use only one mastery per attack. You can use its Bludgeon even without the Weapon Mastery feature, and it does not count against the number of weapons you can use.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Ricochet Barrel)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Your ranged attacks with this blaster ignore Cover if a solid surface is there to bounce the shot toward the target. You can target a creature in Cover with a ricochet shot, but with Disadvantage. As usual, if you only guess where a creature in Cover is and it is not in that space, you miss.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Scope)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A high-magnification scope that improves accuracy at a price in close work. Long range does not give you Disadvantage on ranged attacks with this weapon. But while it is installed, you have Disadvantage on ranged attacks with it out to its normal range.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Silencer)","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A hefty suppressor. Attacks with this blaster make only a faint pew that can be heard out to 10 ft. The light of the shot is hidden too, leaving a flash where it lands and no visible streak in the air.",{}],["Blaster Mod (Thermal Sights)","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A scope with no magnification. While you attack with this blaster, you have Thermalsight out to its normal range. The view is a narrow tunnel, so you have Disadvantage on ability checks that rely on this Thermalsight.",{}],["Blaster Prototype","Weapon","Artifact",1,"The first blaster, built before arcane batteries and powered by a mortal soul. It is a Repeater (2d6 Radiant, range 60/240, Blaster, Firearm, Vex mastery). **Magic Weapon.** It gives a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls. **Auto-Aim.** If you roll below 10 on the d20 for an attack with it, you can replace the roll with a 10. The prototype can decline this, or choose to replace the roll with a 1 if it thinks the target is unsuitable. **Blaster Mastery.** As a Magic action, you can change its mastery to that of any blaster you choose. You can use that mastery even without the Weapon Mastery feature, and it does not count against the number of weapons you can use. Once changed, it cannot change again until the next dawn. **Machine Code.** It can cast the Technomancy cantrip. **Sentience.** It is a sentient Chaotic Neutral weapon with Intelligence 16, Wisdom 10 and Charisma 15. It has hearing and Darkvision out to 120 ft, speaks Common, Dwarvish and Machine Code, and talks to its wielder telepathically. **Personality.** It has the cheerful voice of a young woman who craves new places and people, hates being holstered or ignored, and will not fire on anyone she judges innocent. **Destroying the Blaster.** Its enchantments make it immune to damage. Connecting it to a very large power source, such as a Class 7 or 8 Dark Matter engine at the moment of a void jump, overloads and destroys it.",{"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Repeater"]}],["Bottled Lightning","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A glass canister of magic lightning (50 gp). It sheds Bright Light in a 10-ft radius and Dim Light for 10 ft beyond. When you take the Attack action, you can swap one attack for throwing it. Target one creature or object you see within 20 ft. The target makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 plus your Dexterity modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus) or takes 2d8 Lightning damage and cannot make Opportunity Attacks until the start of its next turn.",{}],["Bounty Hunter's Carbine","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Standard Carbine (2d6 Radiant, range 80/320, Blaster, Firearm, Two-Handed, Slow mastery). You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. **Tracker.** When you hit a creature with it, you can mark the target for 24 hours. While the mark lasts and both are on the same plane, the carbine beeps to show the target's distance. The mark ends if the creature dies or you mark another. **Nonlethal.** When you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points with it, you can knock the target out instead, as with a Melee weapon. **Magic Item Set.** If you carry it and wear a Bounty Hunter's Vest, you can disarm your target with a well-placed shot. When you hit and beat the target's AC by 5 or more, or score a Critical Hit, the target makes a DC 15 Strength save. On a fail it drops one object you choose that it holds, and the object lands at its feet.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Standard Carbine"]}],["Bounty Hunter's Vest","Armor","Uncommon",0,"A Tactical Nanofiber Vest (Light armor, AC 12 plus Dexterity modifier). Its holsters open into an extradimensional space that hides two blasters and a Melee weapon perfectly. You can draw a weapon from it at once, even outside your turn, without spending a Reaction. **Magic Item Set.** If you wear it and carry a Bounty Hunter's Carbine, you can treat your Initiative roll as 10 or as your character level plus your Dexterity modifier, whichever is higher.",{}],["Brass Repeater","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A Repeater (2d6 Radiant, range 60/240, Blaster, Firearm, Vex mastery). When you hit with it and two or more different damage dice show the same number, you can add your Dexterity modifier to the damage. **Upgraded Magic Item.** At character level 5 you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, rising to +2 at level 11 and +3 at level 17.",{"base":["Repeater"]}],["Concussion Grenade","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A sphere covered in blinking lights (200 gp). As a Utilize action, throw it up to 30 ft. At the start of your next turn it detonates in a 10-ft-radius Sphere. It has AC 13 and Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage, and it detonates at once if it takes damage after being thrown. Each creature in the area makes a DC 13 Dexterity save. On a fail it takes 6d6 Thunder damage and is Deafened for 1 minute. On a success it takes half damage and is not Deafened. **Chain Reaction.** If any Concussion Grenades that nobody wears or carries are within the blast when one detonates, they all go off together. The Thunder damage rises by 1d6 and the radius by 5 ft for each grenade, up to 10d6 and a 30-ft-radius Sphere.",{}],["Contractor Nail","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Dueling Laser (2d6 Radiant, range 30/120, Blaster, Cooldown, Firearm, Light, with Slow mastery). When a d6 of its damage shows a 6, you can roll another d6 and add it. You can add at most four d6s to one damage roll. **Magic Item Set.** Once on each of your turns, if you hit a target that was already hit by a Contractor Needle this turn, it takes an extra 2d6 Radiant damage.",{"base":["Dueling Laser"]}],["Contractor Needle","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Swarm Pistol (2d4 Radiant, range 20/60, Blaster, Firearm, Light, Automatic mastery). When a d4 of its damage shows a 4, you can roll another d4 and add it. You can add at most four d4s to one damage roll. **Magic Item Set.** Once on each of your turns, if you hit a target that was already hit by a Contractor Nail this turn, you can make one extra attack against it with this weapon.",{"base":["Swarm Pistol"]}],["Cryogenic Pod","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A capsule for one Medium or smaller creature that supplies air and heat indefinitely. An occupant sets a duration from 1 month to 1,000 years and starts the pod as a Utilize action. Over 1 minute, the pod locks and freezes the creature and the pod's contents. A frozen creature is Unconscious, does not age, and needs no air, food or water. When the time ends, the pod thaws everything over 1 minute and unlocks. If no duration was set, the occupant stays frozen until another creature uses a Utilize action to deactivate and unlock the pod.",{}],["Data Drive","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 1-inch drive (50 gp) that stores any amount of text, images and video. Over 1 minute, you can move data between it and an Arcane Terminal, Datapad or similar computer. You can only upload or download what you have access to, and some data may be encrypted for authorized users. You need a device with an interface, such as a Datapad, to read it.",{}],["Datapad","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A flat rectangular device (50 gp) for everyday computing. It takes notes, shows downloaded data, moves credits to and from the Galactic Bank, and links to other devices. Datapads connect to each other and to Arcane Terminals within 1 mile, so users can talk by text, audio or video and search a connected terminal. On settled worlds, terminals are usually joined in planetary nets that link any two users and give access to vast stores of knowledge.",{}],["Death Ray","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Repeater (2d6 Radiant, range 60/240, Blaster, Firearm, Vex mastery). You gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. While you are attuned, you can use a Magic action to cast Disintegrate (DC 17) from it. Once cast, it cannot be used this way again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"],"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3},"base":["Repeater"]}],["Deck of Holding","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A handheld device with a large screen linked to an extradimensional space. As a Utilize action, touch an object that nobody wears or carries to the deck and it teleports into the space. The object must be under 4 ft across in every dimension and weigh under 150 lb. The deck holds up to 500 lb, not over 64 cubic feet, and its screen shows the contents. As a Utilize action while holding it, pick a stored item and teleport it to your hands or to a free space on the ground within 5 ft. If the deck is destroyed, the contents scatter in the Astral Plane. Putting the deck inside another extradimensional space, such as a Bag of Holding, destroys both and opens a gate to the Astral Plane at that point. Every creature within 10 ft is pulled through to a random place on the Astral Plane, and the gate then closes for good.",{}],["Deck of Holding (Expanded Storage)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A handheld device with a large screen linked to an extradimensional space. As a Utilize action, touch an object that nobody wears or carries to the deck and it teleports into the space. The object must be under 4 ft across in every dimension and weigh under 150 lb. The deck holds up to 500 lb, not over 64 cubic feet, and its screen shows the contents. As a Utilize action while holding it, pick a stored item and teleport it to your hands or to a free space on the ground within 5 ft. If the deck is destroyed, the contents scatter in the Astral Plane. Putting the deck inside another extradimensional space, such as a Bag of Holding, destroys both and opens a gate to the Astral Plane at that point. Every creature within 10 ft is pulled through to a random place on the Astral Plane, and the gate then closes for good. **Expanded Storage.** This deck holds up to 2,000 lb, not over 256 cubic feet.",{}],["Deck of Holding (Password Protected)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A handheld device with a large screen linked to an extradimensional space. As a Utilize action, touch an object that nobody wears or carries to the deck and it teleports into the space. The object must be under 4 ft across in every dimension and weigh under 150 lb. The deck holds up to 500 lb, not over 64 cubic feet, and its screen shows the contents. As a Utilize action while holding it, pick a stored item and teleport it to your hands or to a free space on the ground within 5 ft. If the deck is destroyed, the contents scatter in the Astral Plane. Putting the deck inside another extradimensional space, such as a Bag of Holding, destroys both and opens a gate to the Astral Plane at that point. Every creature within 10 ft is pulled through to a random place on the Astral Plane, and the gate then closes for good. **Password Protected.** The deck is locked to its user's password. Only someone who knows it can store or take items. A DC 18 Intelligence (Data) check hacks the deck and gives unauthorized access.",{}],["Diode Beam","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A two-handed beam weapon with 3 charges that returns all spent charges at dawn. When you take the Attack action, you can spend 1 charge to swap one attack for a 5-ft-wide, 60-ft-long Line in a direction you choose. Each creature in it makes a DC 13 Dexterity save and takes 3d8 Radiant damage on a fail or half on a success. **Upgraded Magic Item.** If you are proficient with Martial weapons, the save DC rises to 15 at level 5, 17 at level 11 and 18 at level 17. You are proficient with it.",{"ch":[3,"3","dawn"]}],["Dome Projector","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"An egg-shaped device. As an action, activate it to raise a dome of force around the projector, as if you had cast Geodesic Shield. When the spell ends, the projector burns out and becomes nonmagical.",{}],["Double Laser Sword","Weapon","Rare",0,"A laser sword whose long hilt projects a second blade from the far end. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it. It has Finesse and Two-Handed (instead of Versatile). Right after you take the Attack action and attack with it, you can use a Bonus Action to make a second melee attack with it. Martial Melee weapon, 1d8 Radiant, Sap mastery.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"wp":{"d":"1d8","t":"Radiant","cat":"M","k":"M","p":"Finesse, Two-Handed","m":"Sap","w":3,"xw":1},"base":["Double Laser Sword"]}],["Drive Wheel","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A steering wheel a foot wide with two handles. Grip it to cast Speedcycle. The motorcycle appears under you and attaches to the wheel. Once used this way, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.",{"ch":[1,"1","dawn"]}],["Drone Controller","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A set of controls built into a glove, a Datapad or a visor. Each controller is linked to one drone that uses the Personal Drone stat block, and it is an Assault, Medical or Shield drone. **Drone Combat.** While you are attuned, you can use a Bonus Action to give the drone orders. It takes its turn right before or right after yours each round, as you choose. With no orders, it takes no actions. Once ordered, it keeps following the order until the task is done.",{}],["Ancestral Laser Sword","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"A Laser Sword or Laser Greatsword handed down through generations, which remembers each past master. When you roll a 1 on an attack roll with it, you can reroll and must use the new roll. **Upgraded Magic Item.** At character level 5 you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, rising to +2 at level 11 and +3 at level 17. **Ancestral Property.** When found, the sword has a property from its last wielder. The GM picks it or rolls for it.",{}],["Arcane Carbine +1","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Standard or Antimatter Carbine. Requires attunement by a spellcaster. While you hold it, you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, to your spell attack rolls and to your spell save DCs.",{"by":"a Spellcaster","fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1,"spellAtk":1}}],["Arcane Carbine +2","Weapon","Very Rare",1,"A Standard or Antimatter Carbine. Requires attunement by a spellcaster. While you hold it, you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus. You gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, to your spell attack rolls and to your spell save DCs.",{"by":"a Spellcaster","fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2,"spellAtk":2}}],["Arcane Carbine +3","Weapon","Legendary",1,"A Standard or Antimatter Carbine. Requires attunement by a spellcaster. While you hold it, you can use it as a Spellcasting Focus. You gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, to your spell attack rolls and to your spell save DCs.",{"by":"a Spellcaster","fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3,"spellAtk":3}}],["Axe of the Mother Tree","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Battleaxe or Greataxe, a traditional skathari axe carved from rough ironwood. When you score a Critical Hit with it, you regain Hit Points equal to the Slashing damage dealt. **Upgraded Magic Item.** At character level 5 you gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls with it, rising to +2 at level 11 and +3 at level 17.",{}],["Blaster for Dummies","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"Any Martial blaster. While you are attuned, you are proficient with it and can use its mastery even without the Weapon Mastery feature, and it does not count against the number of weapons you can use. It has 3 charges and regains all spent charges at dawn. When you miss with a ranged attack from it, you can spend 1 charge to add +5 to the attack roll, which may turn the miss into a hit. A built-in AI cheers when you hit and scolds you when you miss.",{"ch":[3,"3","dawn"]}],["Embedded Mini Fridge","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 75 gp). A chilled compartment in your abdomen holds up to six cans of Krash, potions, or similar drinks.",{}],["Embedded Translator","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot, 150 gp). A Universal Translator is built into your skull. You can use it at will.",{}],["Embedded Weapon","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Arms slot, base weapon price plus 200 gp). Choose a Simple or Martial weapon. It is built into one or both arms. When you draw it, the hand or hands become the weapon and cannot be disarmed of it. A transformed hand cannot hold or use any other weapon, Shield, or object.",{}],["Embedded Weapon +1","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Arms slot, base weapon price plus 750 gp). As Embedded Weapon, with a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1}}],["Embedded Weapon +2","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"Graft (Arms slot, base weapon price plus 5,700 gp). As Embedded Weapon, with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2}}],["Embedded Weapon +3","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"Graft (Arms slot, base weapon price plus 55,200 gp). As Embedded Weapon, with a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it.",{"fx":{"atk":3,"dmg":3}}],["Final Word","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 100,000 gp). A tiny Arcane Warhead inside you is wired to your life. When you die, it detonates and destroys your body, so only True Resurrection or Wish can restore you. Each creature in a 180-ft-radius Sphere centered on you makes a DC 19 Dexterity save. Creatures within 60 ft cannot avoid the damage with Evasion or similar features. A failed save takes 1d4 Mega (1d4 x 100) Force damage, a success takes half.",{}],["Finger Picks","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 800 gp). A mechanical hand holds a retractable set of Thieves' Tools in its fingers. Extend or retract them as a Bonus Action. Retracted, they are perfectly hidden. You have proficiency with Thieves' Tools. If you already had it, double your Proficiency Bonus on checks that use them.",{}],["Golem Arms","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 6,000 gp). Arms taken from a golem or similar Construct. Your reach is 5 ft greater on Melee weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes. You have Advantage on Strength checks and saving throws.",{}],["Hacker Hands","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Arms slot, 150 gp). Fingers that plug into machines and split into smaller digits for fast typing. The graft counts as an Interface Rig. When you fail a hacking attempt, reroll it and keep the new result. You cannot do this again until you finish a Long Rest.",{}],["Heart of Steel","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 350 gp). An automaton's core replaces your heart. You do not need to sleep, and magic cannot put you to sleep. You can finish a Long Rest in 4 hours if you spend them motionless but conscious.",{}],["Heavy Legs","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Legs slot, 500 gp). A mechanical exoskeleton is rooted in your legs. As a Bonus Action, kick a Large or smaller creature within 5 ft with an Unarmed Strike. On a hit, it is pushed 5 ft away from you. You count as one size larger for carrying capacity.",{}],["Impulse Unit","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Legs slot, 750 gp). Thrusters in your legs and back. Once per turn, after you move at least 15 ft in a straight line, you can move up to 10 ft more in that direction without spending movement. Or spend 10 ft of movement to jump 10 ft vertically.",{}],["Infrasight Eyes","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot, 200 gp). Sensor eyes that see in the dark. You have Darkvision with a range of 60 ft.",{"fx":{"dark":60}}],["Laser Eyes","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot, 250 gp). One or both eyes are laser emitters. Ranged weapon, 2d4 Radiant, range 50/200 ft, Vex mastery, Blaster and Firearm properties. You are proficient with it and cannot be disarmed of it. You cannot use it while Blinded.",{"wp":{"d":"2d4","t":"Radiant","cat":"S","k":"R","p":"Blaster, Firearm","m":"Vex","w":0,"r":"50/200","xw":1},"base":["Laser Eyes"]}],["Lazarus Unit","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Internal slot, 6,000 gp). A defibrillator or similar device in your vital organs. If you are dead or at 0 Hit Points at the start of your turn, it shocks you back with 1 Hit Point. It fails if you have no heart, died of old age, or lack vital organs. After it works, it cannot work again until you finish a Long Rest.",{"ch":[1,"1","long"]}],["Logic Unit","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Head slot, 150 gp). A processing unit boosts your brain. Add half your Proficiency Bonus (round down) to Intelligence checks that use a skill you lack proficiency in, if your Proficiency Bonus is not already included. You know Machine Code, the language of machines, and the Technomancy cantrip. Choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as its spellcasting ability when you install it.",{}],["Encyclopedia Multiplanaria","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"A Datapad holding a vast but unindexed store of knowledge. It offers only what it judges useful at the moment. It has 3 charges and regains all of them at dawn. When you take the Study action, spend 1 charge to gain +20 on Intelligence checks you make as part of that action.",{"ch":[3,"all","dawn"]}],["Etheradio","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A 1,000 lb radio standing over 6 ft tall, plus a 3 ft antenna, that sends and receives audio through the Ethereal Plane. **Transmitting.** Utilize action: send up to 10 minutes of audio to a specific Etheradio on the same plane, or to a station. A message to all Etheradios on the plane via an emergency station can be sent once per day. Any message takes 10 minutes to arrive. **Receiving.** It stores the last 10 hours of audio it received. Utilize action: play it back or tune to a station. **Calibration.** It works only when calibrated to its location. This takes 1 hour and must be redone after moving it over 100 miles.",{}],["Exo-Frame","Armor","Rare",1,"A mechanized, bipedal frame weighing over 2,000 lb. You need no armor training, and you don and doff it as a Utilize action. **Armor Class.** Your AC is 18 and Dexterity does not affect it. You can still use a Shield. **Size.** You become Large if smaller. **Mighty.** Advantage on Strength checks and saving throws. **Integrated Battlefists.** It holds two Battlefists, and you are proficient with them. **Life Suit.** It gives the benefits of a Life Suit.",{}],["Finger Gun Glove","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"Requires attunement by a spellcaster. A fingerless glove that lets you cast the Finger Guns cantrip with your spellcasting ability. You can use its mastery property while attuned.",{}],["Flamethrower","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A two-handed nozzle wired to a backpack of arcane batteries. It has 7 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 at dawn. When you take the Attack action, replace one or more attacks with a 15-ft Cone of fire, spending 1 charge per attack replaced. Dexterity save DC 13, 3d6 Fire on a fail, half on a success. **Upgraded.** With Martial weapon proficiency, the DC rises to 15 at level 5, 17 at level 11, and 18 at level 17.",{"ch":[7,"1d6+1","dawn"]}],["Flashback Polaroid","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"An antique camera loaded with 1d6 + 2 blank photos. Magic action: take a picture to cast Flashback. The developed photo shows the events the spell changed. When the last photo is taken, the camera stops being magical.",{}],["Flashbang","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Utilize action: throw it up to 30 ft. A moment after impact it bursts in a 10-ft-radius Sphere. Each creature there makes a DC 13 Constitution save or is Blinded and Deafened until the start of your next turn. A creature that shields its eyes and ears succeeds automatically. Cost 125 gp.",{}],["Freeze Bomb","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Utilize action: throw it up to 30 ft. A moment after impact it bursts in a 10-ft-radius Sphere. Each creature there makes a DC 13 Constitution save. A fail takes 3d8 Cold damage, has Speed 0, and has Disadvantage on attack rolls until the start of your next turn. A success takes half damage only.",{}],["Gamestation","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A small Datapad full of games. If you spend a Short Rest playing on it, you have Advantage on the next ability check you make before you finish a Short or Long Rest.",{}],["Gamma Fragment","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A crystal shard of pure hardlight with 6 charges. It regains 1d6 charges at dawn. When you make a D20 Test, spend charges up to your Proficiency Bonus and add that number to the d20 roll, to a maximum of 20. If you boost an attack roll that deals damage, you can change its damage type to Force. **Set.** Attuning to several Gamma Fragments counts as one attunement. Their charges form one pool that regains 1d6 per fragment at dawn.",{"ch":[6,"1d6","dawn"]}],["Gamma Pendant","Wondrous Item","Artifact",1,"A mithral medallion set with glowing green crystal, once shattered, its Gamma Fragments scattered across the 'Verse. It has 10 charges and regains 1d6 + 4 at dawn. **Incomplete.** You have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. You breathe underwater and in vacuum and ignore extreme heat, cold and pressure. You can cast Lesser Spells from it (save DC 18) at these charge costs: Hardlight Blaster 2, Hardlight Chains 3, Hardlight Construction 5, Hardlight Gauntlet 5, Hardlight Traps 3. **Complete.** With 3 or more Gamma Fragments unified with it, it gains the benefits of all of them, 20 charges, and regains 1d10 + 10 at dawn. You can also cast Greater Spells: Hardlight Frame 7, Orbital Hardlight Cannon 13, Wall of Force 7. Any weapon you wield gets +2 to attack and damage (or its higher bonus) and can deal Force damage or its normal type. You have Advantage on saves against spells. As a Reaction when a creature you see within 60 ft casts a spell, absorb it. The spell has no effect, its casting time is wasted, and the pendant regains charges equal to the spell's level, up to 20. This works once per dawn. **Destruction.** It is impervious to damage, but two hardlight constructs the size of a small planet could crush it.",{"ch":[10,"1d6+4","dawn"]}],["Grasshopper","Weapon","Rare",0,"Dueling Laser. On a hit it deals an extra 2d10 Radiant damage and the target is pushed 10 ft away from you. After you attack with it, it Overheats and cannot attack again until the end of your next turn.",{"base":["Dueling Laser"],"xd":["Hit: +2d10 Radiant and push 10 ft"]}],["Gravity Gun","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"It has 7 charges and regains 1d6 + 1 at dawn. Holding it, use a Magic action and 1 charge to cast Levitate (DC 13). Instead of rising, the target is pulled toward the device and hovers in a space you choose within 5 ft of you. As a Bonus Action, you can hurl a levitating target within 5 ft up to 60 ft in a direction you choose, which ends the spell. If it hits an obstacle, both take 4d6 damage, and the GM picks Bludgeoning, Piercing or Slashing. In Zero Gravity, all creatures and objects count as levitating. **Upgraded.** With Martial weapon proficiency, the DC rises to 15 at level 5, 17 at level 11, and 18 at level 17.",{"ch":[7,"1d6+1","dawn"]}],["Gravity Nullifier","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Magic action: attach this fist-sized device to an object under 2,000 lb. Its mass is nullified as if Levitate targeted it. It works for 10 minutes, then burns out for good. An object still aloft drifts gently to the ground. Cost 50 gp.",{}],["Greater Shipmending Spray","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A 20 lb canister of pressurized nanites. Use it as a Magic action from inside or outside a damaged ship. The ship regains 6d6 Mega Hit Points.",{}],["Hardlight Bracer","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"It has 20 charges and regains 1d10 + 5 at dawn. Magic action, 1 charge: make a Hardlight Dart appear in your open hand. If unused, it fades after 24 hours.",{"ch":[20,"1d10+5","dawn"]}],["Heretical Sunstaff of Ra","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"Avia-Ra Sunstaff. When it deals the Bludgeoning damage of its Bludgeon mastery, it adds 1d6 Radiant. **Upgraded.** You gain +1 to attack and damage with it at level 5, +2 at level 11, and +3 at level 17. **Set.** Attuning to this sunstaff, an Ankh of Ra and Solar Wings of Ra counts as one attunement. With the sunstaff and one other of these, use a Magic action to loose a 5-ft-wide, 60-ft-long Line of light. Each creature in it makes a DC 15 Constitution save or is Blinded until the end of your next turn. This works once per dawn.",{"base":["Avia-Ra Sunstaff"],"xd":["Bludgeon mastery: +1d6 Radiant"]}],["Holo-Companion","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Press the button on this faceted orb as a Magic action to project a translucent humanoid figure around it. The figure works exactly like Unseen Servant, but is visible. Its creator decides its look.",{}],["Holo-Sphere","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Magic action: set this 6-inch Sphere within 15 ft of you. It records holograms of events in a 15-ft Emanation around it, up to 5 minutes in total. As a Magic action, pause recording, delete a scene, or play one back at full size or at 1-ft scale. Magic interferes with recording, and heavy magic can turn playback into a garbled mess. Cost 75 gp.",{}],["Hoverboard","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A 3-ft metal board that hovers over any surface. Mount or dismount as a Bonus Action. While riding it, your Speed rises by 10 ft, you ignore Difficult Terrain, and you can cross liquids without sinking. It cannot climb inclines steeper than 45 degrees outside zero gravity. Use a Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Charisma (Performance) check for tricks.",{}],["Hyper-Krash","Potion","Rare",0,"A discontinued, too-extreme energy drink. When you drink it, you gain an extra action this turn, usable only for the Attack (one attack), Dash, Disengage, Hide or Utilize action. You also have Advantage on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of the turn. Then lethargy sets in, and you cannot gain its benefits again for 1 hour.",{}],["Invisibomb","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Utilize action: throw it up to 30 ft. On impact it bursts in a shimmering 30-ft-radius Sphere. Each creature and each object not worn or carried there is Invisible until the start of your next turn. The condition ends early for a creature once it makes an attack roll, deals damage, or casts a spell.",{}],["Jax","Potion","Rare",0,"Inject it as a Bonus Action. For 1 hour, your Strength and Dexterity each rise by 2, to a maximum of 22. Succeed on a DC 10 Constitution save or have a bad reaction, dropping to 0 Hit Points, falling unconscious, and being unable to regain Hit Points for 1 hour. You can inject up to three doses in the same Bonus Action. Each extra dose raises both scores by a further 2, to a maximum of 26, and adds 5 to the save DC, to a maximum of 25.",{}],["Jetpack","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A small impulse engine on straps with a handheld controller. It has 4 charges and regains 1d4 at dawn. Wear it on your back, then use a Magic action and 1 charge to gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed for 10 minutes.",{"ch":[4,"1d4","dawn"],"fx":{"fly":"walk"}}],["Justiciar's Gavel","Weapon","Uncommon",1,"Rocket Hammer, the badge of office of a dwarven justicar. Once per turn, when you hit with a melee attack using it, fire its thrusters for an extra 1d4 Bludgeoning damage, or 1d6 if the target is Bloodied. **Upgraded.** You gain +1 to attack and damage with it at level 5, +2 at level 11, and +3 at level 17.",{"base":["Rocket Hammer"],"xd":["Once per turn: +1d4 Bludgeoning (1d6 if Bloodied)"]}],["Life Suit","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A one-piece jumpsuit with a domed glass helmet. You breathe underwater and in vacuum for up to 24 hours at a time. It protects against extreme temperatures and pressures, inhaled poisons and gases, and contagions. You can wear it under armor. To refill its air, take it off for 2 hours. Cost 100 gp.",{}],["Motion Tracker","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A scanner with an illuminated screen. Holding it, you learn the location of every creature or object within 60 ft that has moved since the end of your last turn, even if Invisible or behind Cover. A creature Invisible from the Hide action avoids detection.",{}],["Nanobot Canister (Deconstructive)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A capsule of short-lived nanobots. All three kinds look the same, and a DC 15 Intelligence (Technology) check tells which one it holds. Magic action: throw it at a creature, object or empty space within 30 ft. At an empty space, the nanobots cover a 5-ft square. **Deconstructive.** The target makes a DC 15 Dexterity save or is covered. At the start of each of its turns, it takes 1d10 Necrotic damage that ignores Resistance and Immunity. After 1 minute the nanobots shut down for good.",{}],["Nanobot Canister (Reconstructive)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A capsule of short-lived nanobots. All three kinds look the same, and a DC 15 Intelligence (Technology) check tells which one it holds. Magic action: throw it at a creature, object or empty space within 30 ft. At an empty space, the nanobots cover a 5-ft square. **Reconstructive.** The target is covered and regains 1d6 Hit Points at the start of each of its turns. After 1 minute the nanobots shut down for good.",{}],["Ghost Suit","Armor","Rare",1,"Any Light armor can be made as a Ghost Suit. The color shifts to match the surroundings. If you moved 15 ft or less on your turn, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made for the Hide action. You can also Hide while Lightly Obscured.",{"base":["Padded Armor","Leather Armor","Studded Leather Armor"]}],["Golem Skin","Armor","Rare",1,"Any armor can be made as Golem Skin. Glowing attachment points trace its surface. It has four body slots for construct grafts: Arms, External, Head and Legs. While you wear it, you gain the benefits of grafts installed in it and lose those of grafts on your own body, except Internal ones. You can don and doff it as a Bonus Action.",{}],["Hullcutter","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"A Plasma Cutter or Thermal Lance with a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls. When it hits a ship or a Mega creature, it deals 1 Mega Hit Point of damage.",{"fx":{"atk":1,"dmg":1},"base":["Plasma Cutter","Thermal Lance"]}],["Nanobot Canister (Transformative)","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A capsule of short-lived nanobots. A DC 15 Intelligence (Technology) check tells which of the three kinds it holds. Use a Magic action to throw it at a creature, an object or an empty space within 30 ft (an empty space gets a 5-ft square of nanobots).\n**Transformative.** The nanobots form a Nanite Swarm at the impact point. It is friendly to you and your allies, understands your languages and obeys your spoken commands. With no command it takes the Dodge action and moves away from danger. After 8 hours, or when it drops to 0 Hit Points, the nanites deactivate.",{}],["Overdrive Module","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (Internal slot). An internal generator that speeds up your reactions. Use a Bonus Action to start it for 1 minute. When you start it and as a Bonus Action on each later turn, you have Advantage on the next attack roll or ability check you make before your turn ends. You can also use your Reaction to gain Advantage on a Dexterity save or to impose Disadvantage on an attack against you from a creature you can see. Once used, it cannot be started again until you finish a Long Rest.",{}],["Personality Module","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot). A neural trace of a whole personality. While it is installed you are proficient in two skills, know two languages and have one personality trait of the original. Each module is modeled on a different person and gives its own skills, languages and trait.",{}],["Phase Suit","Armor","Rare",1,"A skin-tight suit that shifts you out of phase with the Material Plane (made from Light armor). While attuned, you can move through solid objects and occupied spaces as if they were Difficult Terrain. If you end your turn in such a space, you are shunted to the last unoccupied space you were in.",{}],["Potion of Liquid Air","Potion","Common",0,"For 8 hours after you drink it, you can breathe underwater and in the vacuum of space. It also protects you from extreme temperatures and pressures.",{}],["Potion of Solar Radiance","Potion","Uncommon",0,"An opaque silver liquid that glows when shaken. For 1 hour your body sheds sunlight, Bright Light in a 20-ft radius and Dim Light for 20 ft beyond. Until it ends, you can use a Bonus Action on your turn to deal 1d8 Radiant damage to each creature in the Bright Light.",{}],["Psionic Piercing","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"An exotic crystal piercing (ring, stud, bar or any form, worn anywhere). All your Psionic Piercings count as one attuned item, up to 7 of them. Each one you are attuned to gives you 1 psionic energy point to spend on the properties below. Change your picks daily at dawn. For spells from it, choose Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma as the spellcasting ability.\n**Empathy (1).** Magic action: read the emotional state of a creature you see within 30 ft.\n**Fly (5).** Fly Speed equal to your Speed.\n**Influence (2).** Cast Detect Thoughts and Suggestion once each. Each is then unavailable until the next dawn.\n**Minor Kinesis (1).** Learn Mage Hand. Its hand is invisible.\n**Prescience (2).** Bonus Action: the GM reveals something likely to happen in the next minute, and you have Advantage on D20 Tests about it. Uses equal the number of piercings you are attuned to, all regained at dawn.\n**Psiblast (5).** A 60-ft Cone. Each creature makes an Intelligence save (DC 8 + Proficiency Bonus + your Intelligence, Wisdom or Charisma modifier, your choice). Fail: 6d8 Psychic damage and Stunned for 1 minute. Success: half damage. A Stunned creature repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. Once used, not again until the next dawn.\n**Psychic Resistance (1).** Resistance to Psychic damage.\n**Telepathy (1).** Speak telepathically to a creature you see within 60 ft. It understands only if it knows the language and cannot answer this way.\n**Telekinesis (3).** Cast Telekinesis once without a slot, regained at dawn.\n**Third Eye (3).** Blindsight with a range of 20 ft.",{}],["Rebounding Blade","Weapon","Rare",1,"A Laser Sword with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. It has the Thrown property (range 40/120). Right after any thrown attack, the weapon flies back to your hand.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Laser Sword"]}],["Remote Eye","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot). A spherical mechanical eye replaces one of yours. Remove or insert it as a Bonus Action. While it is out, you still see what it sees as long as you are within 120 ft of it. It looks in every direction but cannot move by itself.",{}],["Remote Piloting Apparatus","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A set of linked devices that takes 1 hour to install in a Fighter-sized ship. The fighter can then be deployed and flown remotely from the included controller, which relays sight and sensor data and lets a character in the Dogfighter role use it. If the ship goes more than 10 miles from the controller, it loses the link and goes dormant until the controller is back in signal range.",{}],["Replacement","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Any slot). An organ or limb swapped for an efficient mechanical one. It can replace a missing limb or organ but cannot revive a dead creature. A replacement limb can look natural or openly metallic. It uses the body slot it fits (a robotic hand takes Arms, a kidney takes Internal). You can have several Replacements in one slot.",{}],["Resistance Plating","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (External slot). A subdermal layer that redirects one kind of elemental energy. While installed you have Resistance to one damage type, picked by the GM or rolled on 1d6: 1 Acid, 2 Cold, 3 Fire, 4 Lightning, 5 Poison, 6 Thunder.",{}],["Ring of Paradoxes","Ring","Legendary",0,"Use a Magic action to spend 1 of its 3 charges and cast Paradox from it. The ring becomes nonmagical when the last charge is spent.",{"ch":[3,"0","never"]}],["Ring of Spacewalking","Ring","Uncommon",1,"While attuned, you can breathe underwater and in the vacuum of space, and you are protected from extreme temperatures and pressures. In zero gravity you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed.",{}],["Scout Scanner","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A device worn over one eye with 3 charges, all regained at dawn. As a Bonus Action, spend 1 charge to analyze a creature you see within 60 ft. You learn two of these: its AC, current Hit Points, Immunities, Resistances, Vulnerabilities, or the spells currently affecting it.",{"ch":[3,"3","dawn"]}],["Shield Emitter","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",1,"A device that wraps you in a shimmering force field. Activate it as a Bonus Action. The next attack against you within the next hour has a -10 penalty to hit. Then it must recharge and cannot be used again until the next dawn.",{}],["Shield Module","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Internal slot). Cast Shield once with it without a spell slot. Once used, it cannot be used again until you finish a Long Rest.",{}],["Shipmending Spray","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 20 lb canister of pressurized nanites. Use a Magic action from inside or outside a damaged ship and the ship regains 3d6 Mega Hit Points.",{}],["Shipmending Sprays","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"A 20 lb canister of pressurized nanites. Use a Magic action from inside or outside a damaged ship and the ship regains Mega Hit Points by rarity: Common 3d6, Greater (Uncommon) 6d6, Superior (Rare) 12d6, Supreme (Very Rare) 18d6.",{}],["Superior Shipmending Spray","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A 20 lb canister of pressurized nanites. Use a Magic action from inside or outside a damaged ship and the ship regains 12d6 Mega Hit Points.",{}],["Supreme Shipmending Spray","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A 20 lb canister of pressurized nanites. Use a Magic action from inside or outside a damaged ship and the ship regains 18d6 Mega Hit Points.",{}],["Shock Absorbers","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Legs slot). Coiled absorbers let you bound higher. Your Long Jump and High Jump distance grows by 10 ft (the extra distance costs movement as normal), and standing jumps carry no penalty. When you fall, use your Reaction to cut the damage by five times your Proficiency Bonus.",{}],["Shoulder Cannon","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"Worn on the back. Speak the command word as a Magic action and a cannon rises above your left shoulder for 1 minute. At the start of each of your turns (no action needed) it attacks the nearest enemy it sees within 60 ft, with a +9 attack bonus, dealing 3d8 Force damage on a hit. It has Darkvision and Thermalsight out to 120 ft and sees Invisible creatures. If you are Incapacitated or die, it stays active until the duration ends. Once activated, it cannot be activated again until the next dawn.",{}],["Singularity Emitter","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A stripped-down Dark Matter engine that launches miniature black holes. It has 5 charges and regains 1d4 + 1 at dawn. While holding it, use a Magic action and spend 1 or more charges to cast Gravity Well from it (save DC 15). One charge casts it at level 3, and each extra charge raises the slot level by 1.",{"ch":[5,"1d4+1","dawn"]}],["Skeleton Keycard","Wondrous Item","Very Rare",0,"A black keycard marked with a white skull. As a Magic action, use it on any door that could be hacked (a ship door, for example), even without a card reader. The door unlocks and opens as if hit by Knock.",{}],["Solar Wings of Ra","Wondrous Item","Rare",1,"A cloak. While you wear it in Bright Light, use a Magic action and speak its command word to turn it into radiant wings until you dismiss them (no action). You gain a Fly Speed of 60 ft, which you lose if you leave Bright Light.\n**Magic Item Set.** Attuning to these wings, an Ankh of Ra and a Heretical Sunstaff of Ra counts as one attunement. While attuned to the wings and one of those items, you can cast Daylight at will with the wings.",{}],["Sorting Beast","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A six-legged machine with eyes, legs and antennae at both ends and measuring tools in the middle. It handles objects up to 30 lb. As a Magic action it collects and sorts all loose valuables within 100 ft, stacking coins in tens and appraising goods like gems by weight and quality, then prints the results on a paper strip. It works until done or switched off (no action). It can also cast Identify with no material components on an object you name, then cannot do so again until the next dawn.",{}],["Spacewalkers","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Legs slot). Creates a zone of breathable air, so you can breathe underwater and in the vacuum of space. It also protects you from extreme temperatures and pressures. In zero gravity you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed.",{}],["Spider Pod","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Throw this metal container as a Magic action and it unfolds into a Mechanical Spider. The spider acts on its own but always obeys you. In combat it takes its turn right before or after yours each round (your choice). If it drops to 0 Hit Points it cannot be repaired. A Magic action folds it back into the pod. You can control at most 3 spiders at once.",{}],["Spiked Skin","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (External slot). A mechanical skin hiding thousands of razor spikes. When a creature you see within 5 ft hits you with a melee attack, use your Reaction to deal 1d4 Piercing damage to it. The damage becomes 2d4 at level 5, 3d4 at level 11 and 4d4 at level 17.",{}],["Tachyon Missile Launcher","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"A shoulder cannon firing heat-seeking missiles built to pierce ship hulls. As a Magic action, lock onto a ship or Mega-sized creature you see within 2,000 ft. The lock breaks if the target moves more than 2,000 ft away or takes Evasive Maneuvers. On a later turn, use a Magic action to fire: make a ranged spell attack with a +9 bonus. On a hit the target takes 3d10 Mega Necrotic damage.",{}],["Terraforming Engine","Wondrous Item","Legendary",0,"A 40-ft-tall machine with great smokestacks that remakes materials and balances an atmosphere. It takes 1 hour of work to turn on or off. Set on a Tier 4 or higher planet and left running for a year to process its water, air and soil, it lowers the planet's Tier by 1. It does nothing on a Tier 1 or Tier X world, and two engines cannot lower a planet's Tier by more than 1 (extra engines only add backup). If it is stopped or removed, the planet returns to its old state over 7 days.",{}],["Thermalsight Eyes","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"Graft (Head slot). Heat-sensing augments in your eyes give you Thermalsight with a range of 30 ft.",{}],["Thunder Rifle","Weapon","Rare",0,"A Concussion Rifle with a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. When it hits a target, it makes an explosion in a 5-ft Emanation around that target. You can also aim it at an empty space within range. Each creature in the area makes a DC 15 Dexterity save, taking half the Thunder damage rolled on a failure and none on a success.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["Concussion Rifle"]}],["Titan Armor","Wondrous Item","Rare",0,"Graft (External slot). Plating built into your body like a suit of armor. Your base AC is 17 and your Dexterity modifier does not affect it. You can wear armor over it and use either armor for your AC. You can still use a Shield and gain this benefit.",{}],["Traction Spikes","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Legs slot). Retractable spikes in your legs let you ignore Difficult Terrain and give you Advantage on saves to avoid the Prone condition.",{}],["Un's Codex","Wondrous Item","Artifact",1,"A 6-inch mechanical disc of countless layered parts, an intricate puzzle made of the exotic metal found in Maw stations and the Sepulcher Star. Its making is credited to Old Un.\n**Solving the Codex.** Until solved, attuning gives no benefits. Spend 8 hours attuned to solve part of it and unlock one property of your choice. Unlocks apply only to you.\n**Blink Step.** Cast Misty Step without a slot. You may teleport into a creature's space. That creature makes a DC 17 Dexterity save. Fail: 4d6 Force damage and it is pushed to the nearest free space. Success: half damage and you move to the nearest free space instead.\n**Extradimensional Lodge.** You and up to six willing creatures within 30 ft are moved to a demiplane holding a large, comfortable lodge in a coniferous forest. Leaving the lodge returns you to where you entered. It has many floors, hidden compartments, secret passages, old nonmagical gear from past owners, and dozens of near-transparent servants who obey all who enter. They do any ordinary servant task but cannot attack, harm anyone or leave the lodge.\n**Magic Resistance.** Advantage on saves against spells and other magical effects.\n**Slip Gate.** 4 charges, 1 regained at dawn. As a Magic action, create two 10-ft circular portals at places you know (or a general place such as a named Maw) on the same plane. They float just above the ground, filled with sight-blocking mist. Anything entering the front of one exits the other. They last 1 minute or until you dismiss them on your turn (no action).\n**Universal Function.** Magic action: rewrite a law of the universe in a 15-ft Emanation from you for 1 minute or until you use this again. You can raise or lower gravity, change a material's boiling or melting point, speed or slow time in the area (Haste or Slow for all creatures inside), make the area breathable (as Zone of Atmosphere), or change another law at the GM's discretion. If the change is too fundamental, such as reversing time, nothing happens and the action is wasted.\n**Destroying the Codex.** It cannot be damaged. Only Old Un can destroy it, but throwing it into the Sepulcher Star or any black hole banishes it for 1d100 years, after which it reappears somewhere in the 'Verse.",{"ch":[4,"1","dawn"]}],["Universal Translator","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A handheld device for long voyages. While holding it, you understand any spoken language you hear. When you speak or sign, any creature that knows at least one language and can hear or see you understands you.",{}],["Vari-Blaster","Weapon","Rare",0,"Any Blaster can be made a Vari-Blaster. It holds five power cells in a rotating set. As a Bonus Action, switch its damage type to Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic or Radiant. It deals an extra 1d6 damage of the chosen type to any target it hits.",{}],["Voice Changer","Wondrous Item","Common",0,"Graft (Head slot). An electronic modulator replaces your vocal cords. You can change pitch, tone and character of your voice at will, flawlessly copy any voice or sound you have heard, and add synthetic effects such as reverb.",{}],["Void Beacon","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A beacon that sends an ultra-high-frequency signal through the Void, detectable tens of thousands of light-years away. The signal holds its current coordinates and a message of up to 16 characters (spaces count). Change the message as a Magic action. Once active, it repeats the signal for 7 days and then burns out for good.",{}],["W-REC","Weapon","Rare",1,"A REC Gun loaded with dozens of absurd and unneeded modifications. It has a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls. It gains the Automatic mastery in addition to Mounted. If you are proficient with it, you can use both mastery properties even without the Weapon Mastery feature, and it does not count against your number of weapons. Once on each of your turns, if you attack a target with it and hit two or more times, you can attack the same target again. That attack has Disadvantage no matter what. If it hits, attack again, and so on, to a total of five attacks against the target or until you miss.",{"fx":{"atk":2,"dmg":2},"base":["REC Gun"]}],["Weapon Wheel","Wondrous Item","Uncommon",0,"A bracer with a rotary dial and buttons, linked to nine tiny extradimensional spaces. While wearing it, use a Magic action to store a weapon or object you hold (up to 100 lb and small enough for a 10-ft cube) in one space and link it to the wheel. It links up to 9 items. A Magic action unlinks one. Once on each of your turns (no action), teleport one linked item to your hand. Any other linked items go back to their spaces.",{}],["Zipgun","Weapon","Uncommon",0,"An Antimatter Pistol built to fire only once, at far above normal power. On a hit it deals 6d6 Necrotic damage. After firing, it smolders, stops being magical and becomes unusable.",{"base":["Antimatter Pistol"]}]];
var ISP={"Death Ray":{"sp":[["Disintegrate",0]],"dc":17},"Dome Projector":{"sp":[["Geodesic Shield",0]]},"Drive Wheel":{"sp":[["Speedcycle",0]]},"Gravity Gun":{"sp":[["Levitate",1]],"dc":13},"Ring of Paradoxes":{"sp":[["Paradox",1]]},"Singularity Emitter":{"sp":[["Gravity Well",1]]}};
var WPN=["Arm Blade", "Arm Cannon", "Double Laser Sword", "Laser Eyes"];
var GR=[["Adamant Hardsuit",1500,65,"Armor","Heavy armor, AC 18. Needs Strength 15. Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Carbonic Suit",50,20,"Armor","Medium armor, AC 13 plus Dexterity modifier (max 2)."],["Environ Suit",10,12,"Armor","Medium armor, AC 12 plus Dexterity modifier (max 2)."],["Ferrofiber Hardsuit",30,40,"Armor","Heavy armor, AC 14. Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Flight Jacket",5,8,"Armor","Light armor, AC 11 plus Dexterity modifier. Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Hexaplate Suit",750,40,"Armor","Medium armor, AC 15 plus Dexterity modifier (max 2). Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Monoplate Suit",50,45,"Armor","Medium armor, AC 14 plus Dexterity modifier (max 2). Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Nanofiber Vest",10,10,"Armor","Light armor, AC 11 plus Dexterity modifier."],["Starshield Hardsuit",200,60,"Armor","Heavy armor, AC 17. Needs Strength 15. Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Tactical Carbonic Hardsuit",75,55,"Armor","Heavy armor, AC 16. Needs Strength 13. Stealth checks have Disadvantage."],["Tactical Nanofiber Vest",45,13,"Armor","Light armor, AC 12 plus Dexterity modifier."],["Triplate Suit",400,20,"Armor","Medium armor, AC 14 plus Dexterity modifier (max 2)."],["Bandolier",3,1,"Adventuring Gear","A shoulder strap with six pouches, each big enough for a potion, grenade or similar item you can reach fast. It holds 10 lb of gear."],["Binoculars",10,0.5,"Adventuring Gear","Whatever you view through them looks ten times larger."],["Comm Set",10,1,"Adventuring Gear","A handheld radio. You can talk by voice with any creature within 1 mile who also has a Comm Set. It can plug into an ear headset or be spoken into directly. The signal passes most barriers but is stopped by 1 ft of stone, 1 inch of common metal, a thin sheet of lead, or 3 ft of wood or dirt."],["AI Core",800,0,"Ship System","A ship system. The Arcane Terminal of your ship gains a sentient AI that keeps the ship running and warns the crew of danger. It has Intelligence 17, Wisdom 13 and Charisma 14, and is proficient in Data and Technology (+2 Proficiency Bonus). It has a +3 modifier on D20 Tests that use Strength, Dexterity or Constitution. It can take the Study action and share what it knows. It can fill any Crew Role aboard and take any action that role offers. It acts at the end of the Initiative order. Its personality varies from prankster to coldly logical."],["Arcane Cannon",700,0,"Ship System","A ship system that magnifies a spellcaster's power so they can cast Mega spells. The Gunner uses it with the Arcane Cannon action."],["Captain's Chair",750,0,"Ship System","A ship system. The ship gains the Captain Crew Role."],["Cloaking",3000,0,"Ship System","A ship system with 6 charges that regains 1d6 expended charges at dawn. The Engineer can use the Use System action to spend 1 charge and make the ship Invisible for 1 minute. The effect ends at once if the ship attacks, deals damage, or moves more than 1,000 ft on its turn."],["Engineer's Pack",198,41,"Adventuring Gear","Holds a Backpack, Comm Set, Crowbar, Datapad, Flashlight, Hammer, Igniter, Life Suit, a handful of nuts and bolts, an Omnitool, 10 rolls of Vent Tape and a Wristwatch."],["Marine's Pack",286,68,"Adventuring Gear","Holds a Backpack, Bedroll, Binoculars, Comm Set, Concussion Grenade, Crowbar, Flashlight, Igniter, Life Suit, 10 days of Rations, Rope, a Tactical Vest and a roll of Vent Tape."],["Flare",1,1,"Adventuring Gear","Utilize action: strike the base to light it. It burns 10 minutes with Bright Light in a 40-ft radius and Dim Light 20 ft farther. It burns underwater and in vacuum."],["Flashlight",10,1,"Adventuring Gear","Casts a 60-ft Cone of Bright Light and Dim Light 15 ft farther. It runs 4 hours, then needs 8 hours to recharge."],["Gaming Set (Digital Games)",0,0,"Gaming Set","A Gaming Set variant playable on any Arcane Terminal, Datapad or Gamestation. The games range from arcade-like to fully immersive."],["Holster",1,0.5,"Adventuring Gear","Lets you carry a blaster that lacks the Two-Handed property on a belt or under the arm."],["Hypodermic Needle",0.5,0,"Adventuring Gear","Load a potion into it as a Bonus Action, then give it to another creature as a Bonus Action. An unwilling target avoids it with a Dexterity save (DC 8 + your Intelligence modifier + your Proficiency Bonus)."],["Igniter",5,0,"Adventuring Gear","Makes a small flame that lights a Candle, Torch or campfire."],["Interface Rig",25,3,"Adventuring Gear","Everything needed to connect to a device with no accessible interface: a Datapad accessor with algorithms, wires and connectors, and a heavy magnet for emergencies. Often needed for unauthorized access."],["Krash",0.16,1.5,"Adventuring Gear","Utilize action: drink it. For 1 hour, your Exhaustion level counts as 1 lower, to a minimum of 0. Only one can work on you at a time."],["Log Keeper",10,3,"Adventuring Gear","A foot-long recorder that stores audio sorted by date. It holds 72 hours, then deletes the oldest entries first."],["Engineer's Station",3000,0,"Ship System","The ship gains the Engineer role."],["Escape Pods",600,0,"Ship System","A bay with enough pods for every crew member and passenger. Utilize action: board a pod and eject. On a Fighter, the Pilot ejects automatically when the ship reaches 0 Mega Hit Points. A pod clears any explosion, then drifts. Its thrusters allow two or three course changes, and it sustains one passenger for 7 days with air, power and rations. It sends a distress signal that ships with Sensors can detect, at light speed. A pod and passenger survive reentry on most planets."],["Fighter Bay",850,0,"Ship System","The ship can dock a Fighter-size ship inside. As a Bonus Action, a creature boards the Fighter, ejects it and becomes its Pilot. A Fighter docks in a bay as an action. **Repeatable.** Install it more than once: Transport 2 bays, Corvette 3, Frigate 3, Cruiser 4, Capital 4."],["Gunner Bay",500,0,"Ship System","The ship gains the Gunner role. **Repeatable.** You can install it more than once."],["Life Support",400,0,"Ship System","Gives the ship air, heat and artificial gravity. If disabled, a backup supplies air and heat for up to 1 hour, but not gravity. On unusual ships, such as galleons, it wraps the whole ship in heat and atmosphere. An Engineer, or a creature that hacks the ship computer, can take the Use System action to disable it. That can vent atmosphere from parts of the ship, switch off gravity (making the ship a Zero-Gravity space in space), or shut off heating and cooling."],["Manipulators",550,0,"Ship System","Collapsible arms, tentacles or hull extensions. An Engineer can take the Use System action to use them on a target within 500 ft. They can carry an object into the cargo hold, clear debris, open a hatch on a ship, or push a Mega target smaller than the ship up to 1,000 ft away."],["Omnitool",10,1,"Adventuring Gear","A multipurpose gadget packed with small knives, a small hammer, screwdrivers, a file, a bottle opener, a small saw, a wrench, a can opener, a wire-cutter and pliers."],["Quadcorder",75,1,"Adventuring Gear","A handheld scanner with four small radar-dish sensors. Aim it at an object within 5 ft as a Utilize action to read its temperature, density, boiling point, freezing point, conductivity and viscosity."],["Researcher's Pack",377,35,"Adventuring Gear","Holds a Backpack, Binoculars, a Comm Set, a Datapad, a Flashlight, a Holo-Sphere, a Hypodermic Needle, a Life Suit, a Log Keeper, an Omnitool, a Quadcorder and a Wristwatch."],["Roach",100,0,"Adventuring Gear","A ten-legged insectoid (Ocoulori Radavitis). Eating one brings a rush of euphoria that lets you see the whole universe at once and improves the result of a void jump. Long-term use is addictive and psychologically harmful."],["Sling",0.5,0,"Adventuring Gear","A strap worn on the body and attached to a weapon, usually a blaster. A weapon you drop while it is slung falls to your side and stays within reach."],["Spacer's Pack",241,29,"Adventuring Gear","Holds a Backpack, a Bandolier, a Comm Set, a Datapad, 2 Flashlights, a Holo-Sphere, an Interface Rig, 2 cans of Krash, a Life Suit, a Log Keeper, an Igniter, an Omnitool, a Quadcorder, 10 rolls of Vent Tape and a Wristwatch."],["Surveyor's Pack",237,66,"Adventuring Gear","Holds a Backpack, a Bandolier, a Bedroll, Binoculars, a Comm Set, a Flashlight, a Log Keeper, an Igniter, a Life Suit, a Quadcorder, 10 days of Rations, Rope and a Wristwatch."],["Tactical Vest",15,6,"Adventuring Gear","A light vest covered in pouches, straps and holsters, worn over armor. It carries one Melee weapon with the Two-Handed or Versatile property on the back and a Dagger or Antimatter Dagger on the front. It has two Holsters and one built-in Sling."],["Vent Tape",0.1,0.5,"Adventuring Gear","Durable adhesive tape, 60 ft of 2-inch-wide tape per roll. Used for quick repairs, or to fix a Flashlight to a blaster in a pinch."],["Wristwatch",5,0,"Adventuring Gear","A simple watch that tells time in a way all major galactic factions accept."],["Pilot's Seat",400,0,"Ship System","Adds the Pilot role to the ship. Repeatable: a Personal-size or larger ship can hold two. If more than one creature is in the Pilot role, they must take different actions each combat round."],["Probe",450,0,"Ship System","A remotely piloted drone launched from the ship to inspect hazardous targets and places. The Engineer uses the Use System action to launch, dock or control it. It has 5 Mega Hit Points, AC 12, Speed 1,500 ft and 360-degree Maneuverability. The Engineer sees and hears through it and reads data such as temperature, gravity and radiation."],["Sensors",400,0,"Ship System","Lets the ship perceive ships and obstacles and talk with other ships (audio, video, holo) out to 1,000 miles. With Sensors disabled, the ship has Disadvantage on attack rolls.\n**Deep Scan.** The Engineer uses Use System on an object of interest within 1 mile and makes an Intelligence (Investigation) check. On a success, they learn of lifesigns inside, whether it has working power, and other details the GM picks.\n**Planetary Scan.** The Engineer uses Use System on a planet within 1,000 miles and makes an Intelligence (Investigation) check. On a success, they learn of major environmental hazards, whether the surface is inhabited, and other details the GM picks."],["Shield Generator",500,0,"Ship System","Projects a directional shield around the ship, forward-facing by default. The Engineer can reposition it as a Bonus Action. If it is disabled, the ship loses all Shield Points until repaired. Shield Points depend on ship size (Shield Points table)."],["Signal Jammer",2500,0,"Ship System","The Engineer uses Use System to jam the Sensors of a ship within 3,000 ft. That ship makes a Wisdom save (DC 8 + the Engineer's Intelligence modifier + Proficiency Bonus). On a failure its Sensors are disabled until the start of the Engineer's next turn, and it has Disadvantage on attack rolls for that time."],["Teleporters",2000,0,"Ship System","Powers a permanent set of Teleportation Circles for short-range transport. The Engineer uses Use System to open a temporary destination circle at an unmoving location within 100 miles. It lasts 1 minute or until another is made. A working Dark Matter engine disrupts the magic, so you cannot make a destination circle inside a ship with a running engine unless both ships agree to allow it.\n**Repeatable.** A Frigate-size or larger ship can install this twice. The second set is always active and speeds travel around the ship."],["Tractor Beam",1000,0,"Ship System","Pulls ships and objects toward your ship. The Engineer uses Use System on a Mega-sized ship, object or creature within 3,000 ft. A Mega creature or ship makes a Dexterity save (DC 8 + the Engineer's Strength or Intelligence modifier + Proficiency Bonus), and anything larger than your ship passes automatically. On a failure the target is caught and pulled up to 1,000 ft closer, with Speed 0. At the start of each of the Engineer's turns, a Utilize action pulls it up to 1,000 ft closer. The target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns and escapes on a success."]];
